27
00:03:41,795 --> 00:03:43,115
I caught you.

28
00:03:46,895 --> 00:03:48,655
Hang on.

29
00:03:49,885 --> 00:03:51,235
Hang on.

30
00:03:52,455 --> 00:03:53,955
Are you okay?

31
00:03:53,955 --> 00:03:55,835
My valiant.

32
00:03:57,465 --> 00:03:59,215
Osman.

33
00:03:59,385 --> 00:04:02,495
I would make you food for crows...

34
00:04:03,465 --> 00:04:08,025
but this cave has become your tomb.

35
00:04:17,815 --> 00:04:19,175
Olof.

36
00:04:19,255 --> 00:04:21,005
We searched everywhere.

37
00:04:21,274 --> 00:04:23,405
There is no other exit to this cave.

38
00:04:24,495 --> 00:04:26,045
Saga.

39
00:04:26,675 --> 00:04:28,795
I avenge you, my brother.

40
00:04:33,365 --> 00:04:38,495
I was going to stick this
dagger into your heart, Osman...

41
00:04:39,385 --> 00:04:43,575
but now I will leave it at your grave.

42
00:04:51,475 --> 00:04:53,975
What will we do if the
enemy is leaderless?

43
00:04:54,005 --> 00:04:55,785
We'll raid his country...

44
00:04:55,815 --> 00:05:00,205
and we kill the scattered
soldiers with the sword...

45
00:05:00,225 --> 00:05:01,635
and we attack his flocks...

46
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:04,125
and we make all the people slaves..

47
00:05:04,125 --> 00:05:06,485
and we kill them all with an axe.

48
00:05:07,365 --> 00:05:09,995
If the enemy does not have a
leader, they will scatter.

49
00:05:09,995 --> 00:05:11,575
and the scattered enemy...

50
00:05:11,575 --> 00:05:13,095
becomes our bait.

51
00:05:14,425 --> 00:05:18,285
Osman's death will turn
Yenişehir upside down.

52
00:05:18,945 --> 00:05:21,025
After this mess...

53
00:05:21,025 --> 00:05:24,305
our storm will destroy Yenişehir...

54
00:05:25,475 --> 00:05:27,025
...but first...

55
00:05:28,705 --> 00:05:31,055
we'll make sure he's dead.

56
00:05:33,575 --> 00:05:35,215
Let some men stay here.

57
00:05:36,215 --> 00:05:40,005
If the impossible happens and
someone gets out of here...

58
00:05:40,755 --> 00:05:42,445
let them kill them.

59
00:05:42,735 --> 00:05:45,535
Osman is dead, Olof.

60
00:05:45,955 --> 00:05:48,275
Why would we leave our men here?

61
00:05:48,275 --> 00:05:50,805
We'll make sure he's dead.

62
00:05:51,715 --> 00:05:54,315
In order not to overshadow our victory.

63
00:05:56,575 --> 00:05:58,705
These guys are not for him...

64
00:05:58,705 --> 00:06:01,125
but for the sake of whoever
comes to take him out.

65
00:06:05,745 --> 00:06:07,085
Come on.

66
00:06:11,275 --> 00:06:12,805
You both.

67
00:06:12,845 --> 00:06:14,405
Wait here.

68
00:06:15,575 --> 00:06:17,155
Sarıca.

69
00:06:27,855 --> 00:06:29,355
Sarıca.

70
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:39,115
Sarıca.

71
00:06:40,495 --> 00:06:43,035
Thank Allah.

72
00:06:43,365 --> 00:06:44,725
Come on.

73
00:06:47,705 --> 00:06:50,115
Come on.

74
00:06:52,955 --> 00:06:54,705
Hang on.

75
00:07:00,135 --> 00:07:02,955
Hang on.

76
00:07:05,255 --> 00:07:07,025
Make a sound, brother Boran.

77
00:07:07,915 --> 00:07:09,305
Brother.

78
00:07:09,365 --> 00:07:10,935
Boran.

79
00:07:11,465 --> 00:07:13,025
Say something.

80
00:07:13,025 --> 00:07:14,545
Boran.

81
00:07:19,525 --> 00:07:21,685
Come on, brother.

82
00:07:30,885 --> 00:07:32,395
Brother.

83
00:07:34,615 --> 00:07:36,185
Boran.

84
00:07:36,415 --> 00:07:38,665
No, no, make a sound, Boran.

85
00:07:38,665 --> 00:07:40,535
Make a sound, Boran.

86
00:07:40,635 --> 00:07:42,145
My Allah, help us.

87
00:07:42,145 --> 00:07:43,525
My Allah.

88
00:07:43,525 --> 00:07:45,685
Grant us your mercy, my Allah.

89
00:07:45,685 --> 00:07:48,215
Save my valiants.

90
00:07:48,215 --> 00:07:50,775
Boran.

91
00:07:50,825 --> 00:07:54,105
Brother, don't you hear?

92
00:07:54,885 --> 00:07:57,675
Make a sound, Boran.

93
00:07:57,675 --> 00:08:00,325
Make a sound, make a sound, brother.

94
00:08:01,205 --> 00:08:04,245
Boran, Boran.

95
00:08:04,245 --> 00:08:07,085
Brother, get up, get up, get up.

96
00:08:07,475 --> 00:08:09,935
Get up, stay awake.

97
00:08:10,285 --> 00:08:13,175
Thank Allah.

98
00:08:13,175 --> 00:08:14,525
My Allah.

99
00:08:14,525 --> 00:08:16,715
Thank Allah.

100
00:08:17,695 --> 00:08:21,975
Pull yourself together.

101
00:08:24,305 --> 00:08:26,425
- Hold on, brother.
- Boran.

102
00:08:29,275 --> 00:08:31,255
Look at me, are you okay?

103
00:08:31,355 --> 00:08:32,605
You are awake, right?

104
00:08:32,605 --> 00:08:34,605
I'm good.

105
00:08:34,895 --> 00:08:38,085
He's still alive, my brother.

106
00:08:43,265 --> 00:08:45,135
Hold on, my brothers, hold on.

107
00:08:45,195 --> 00:08:46,745
This will not kill us.

108
00:08:46,745 --> 00:08:48,005
However...

109
00:08:48,005 --> 00:08:51,525
what will revive us is determination.

110
00:08:51,625 --> 00:08:53,015
Hang on.

111
00:08:55,065 --> 00:08:57,095
This place is closed.

112
00:08:58,045 --> 00:08:59,875
There must be some way out.

113
00:09:00,975 --> 00:09:02,855
There must be some way out.

114
00:09:08,805 --> 00:09:10,875
Yenişehir

115
00:09:12,665 --> 00:09:14,175
Malhun Hatun.

116
00:09:14,175 --> 00:09:15,235
Bala Hatun.

117
00:09:15,235 --> 00:09:17,775
Is there news about Osman Bey?

118
00:09:17,785 --> 00:09:21,315
No news, he was supposed to come by now.

119
00:09:28,145 --> 00:09:29,965
The news that came at night.

120
00:09:32,035 --> 00:09:36,065
Beware that they have used Konur
Alp to lure Osman Bey into a trap.

121
00:09:37,855 --> 00:09:40,875
Prepare the warriors, we are
going to take Osman Bey.

122
00:09:51,145 --> 00:09:53,165
There must be some way out.

123
00:09:54,955 --> 00:09:56,985
There must be some way out.

124
00:09:57,895 --> 00:09:59,235
Hang on.

125
00:10:00,085 --> 00:10:01,835
Hang on, my dear Boran.

126
00:10:01,835 --> 00:10:03,345
Sarıca.

127
00:10:03,725 --> 00:10:05,595
- Baysungur.
- My Bey.

128
00:10:08,975 --> 00:10:11,255
Brother Boran, are you okay?

129
00:10:11,255 --> 00:10:12,605
Brother.

130
00:10:15,565 --> 00:10:18,105
- Brother.
- Oh, brother.

131
00:11:01,165 --> 00:11:03,185
Give me strength, my Allah.

132
00:11:04,305 --> 00:11:05,845
Do your best.

133
00:11:06,205 --> 00:11:08,255
Do your best.

134
00:11:28,865 --> 00:11:30,605
Hang on, Osman.

135
00:11:31,805 --> 00:11:33,595
We will not stay here.

136
00:11:34,615 --> 00:11:36,395
We've gone through many things.

137
00:11:38,065 --> 00:11:40,155
We overcame many difficulties.

138
00:11:54,185 --> 00:11:58,385
I am not fighting a war that has
begun, but I am starting a war.

139
00:12:11,735 --> 00:12:15,725
Whoever harms us will pay the
price for that many times over.

140
00:12:20,815 --> 00:12:23,825
You will always be one body.

141
00:12:24,055 --> 00:12:26,835
You support each other.

142
00:12:32,825 --> 00:12:34,585
For Alps.

143
00:12:36,225 --> 00:12:37,995
And for the sake of children.

144
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:50,455
And for a country that will live forever.

145
00:12:51,885 --> 00:12:53,965
Do your best.

146
00:13:00,135 --> 00:13:01,655
Konur.

147
00:13:02,625 --> 00:13:03,975
Brother.

148
00:13:04,265 --> 00:13:05,815
Hang on.

149
00:13:06,365 --> 00:13:07,665
Hang on.

150
00:13:07,855 --> 00:13:11,155
Come on, hang on, brother.

151
00:13:12,235 --> 00:13:13,545
Come on.

152
00:13:14,635 --> 00:13:15,965
Brother

153
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:22,995
Get up, come on.

154
00:13:23,985 --> 00:13:26,265
You will be fine.

155
00:13:27,385 --> 00:13:29,755
Konur, my brother.

156
00:13:29,885 --> 00:13:31,925
You'll be fine, brother.

157
00:13:33,985 --> 00:13:35,335
Come.

158
00:14:07,395 --> 00:14:09,425
Come on, brother.

159
00:14:09,615 --> 00:14:11,655
Come on, drink it.

160
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:17,555
You will be fine.

161
00:14:25,195 --> 00:14:27,255
In the name of of Allah the Merciful.

162
00:14:34,675 --> 00:14:36,205
O Allah.

163
00:14:39,115 --> 00:14:40,815
Hang on, brother.

164
00:14:42,925 --> 00:14:44,335
Hang on.

165
00:14:46,945 --> 00:14:48,015
Brother.

166
00:14:48,865 --> 00:14:50,355
You will be fine.

167
00:14:58,575 --> 00:15:01,885
Hang on, Osman.

168
00:15:05,625 --> 00:15:06,975
Hang on.

169
00:15:11,045 --> 00:15:12,795
My Bey.

170
00:15:12,895 --> 00:15:15,795
- We won't leave you alone.
- You're all right, aren't you?

171
00:15:29,105 --> 00:15:31,105
Yenişehir

172
00:15:31,575 --> 00:15:34,825
Look under every stone, Bala,
and find Osman Bey.

173
00:15:34,885 --> 00:15:37,695
We'll find him, Malhun, we'll find
him, don't worry.

174
00:15:38,315 --> 00:15:42,165
Be careful, those who play
games against Osman Bey will not stop.

175
00:15:42,315 --> 00:15:45,325
- Enemies surround us on every side.
- Don't worry.

176
00:15:47,345 --> 00:15:50,175
What if something bad
happened to my father?

177
00:15:51,385 --> 00:15:52,775
what shall we do?

178
00:15:53,925 --> 00:15:57,865
We'll do what Osman Bey
would do in a situation like this.

179
00:15:59,455 --> 00:16:04,245
Sons, we are now in the most
difficult times and we will unite.

180
00:16:04,595 --> 00:16:06,725
And we will be stronger than ever.

181
00:16:07,385 --> 00:16:08,815
We will not despair.

182
00:16:09,065 --> 00:16:12,885
We will cling to hope and protect
Osman Bey's trust as we should.

183
00:16:15,745 --> 00:16:18,915
Aktemur, increase the number of Alps
in Yenişehir.

184
00:16:19,135 --> 00:16:24,175
Put five warriors in the place where you put two of them, we will not allow the passage of the infidels.

185
00:16:25,195 --> 00:16:30,085
And tell all Beys to come, and we
will quickly convene the court.

186
00:16:31,145 --> 00:16:34,095
If Osman Bey is not here, his son is.

187
00:16:37,605 --> 00:16:41,205
- Orhan Bey, Bey of Karacahisar.
- Yes, mother.

188
00:16:41,575 --> 00:16:46,865
You will deputize for Osman Bey in
the court as the Bey of Karacahisar.

189
00:16:48,455 --> 00:16:51,135
Do you agree with that, Bala Hatun?

190
00:16:51,985 --> 00:16:55,385
Orhan Bey can fulfill this task properly.

191
00:16:55,895 --> 00:16:57,775
I agree, Malhun Hatun.

192
00:16:59,715 --> 00:17:02,675
And what do you think, Alaaddin Bey?

193
00:17:03,195 --> 00:17:06,295
If Osman Bey was here, he would have
ordered it, Malhun mother.

194
00:17:06,414 --> 00:17:08,763
The head of the Court is
my brother's right.

195
00:17:10,233 --> 00:17:13,714
Your command is like Osman Bey's
command, mother.

196
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:20,365
So, Orhan Bey is the one
who will head the court.

197
00:17:23,825 --> 00:17:27,474
And the system will run in Yenişehir
as if Osman Bey is completely there.

198
00:17:29,295 --> 00:17:33,655
Come back with the good news, Bala.

199
00:17:33,895 --> 00:17:36,825
- May Allah help us
- Amin.

200
00:17:43,305 --> 00:17:46,825
I entrusted you to Allah! Come on, Alps.

201
00:17:58,435 --> 00:17:59,565
Come on.

202
00:18:04,315 --> 00:18:07,705
My Allah, be with them.

203
00:18:16,445 --> 00:18:18,775
I have brought the
fabrics you requested.

204
00:18:19,555 --> 00:18:23,025
But I think the time is not right.

205
00:18:23,325 --> 00:18:26,515
No, you came just in time, Marta

206
00:18:28,315 --> 00:18:32,195
Let the Alps pay you, but
you must go nowhere.

207
00:18:33,795 --> 00:18:37,075
I mean, don't run
around, I'll pass you by.

208
00:19:07,095 --> 00:19:09,855
You're late, Kantakuzenos.

209
00:19:10,245 --> 00:19:12,935
I'm never late, Olof, speak up.

210
00:19:13,695 --> 00:19:16,025
I buried Osman alive in the dirt.

211
00:19:16,585 --> 00:19:18,705
He is now at the table of demons.

212
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:21,515
Now it's all Turks' turn.

213
00:19:22,475 --> 00:19:24,555
Did he die? And how did that happen?

214
00:19:25,165 --> 00:19:30,245
Osman came to save that dog named Sarkis.

215
00:19:31,065 --> 00:19:34,945
I demolished a large
cave over their heads.

216
00:19:35,955 --> 00:19:39,425
Olof, Osman has devilish tricks.

217
00:19:39,905 --> 00:19:44,695
Even if Osman is the devil, he won't emerge
from under the rubble of those stones.

218
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:51,315
Do not worry! They died like rats inside.

219
00:19:52,015 --> 00:19:54,635
Even their corpses could not be obtained.

220
00:19:55,055 --> 00:19:58,545
And my men surround that cave.

221
00:20:00,575 --> 00:20:03,905
Osman has found the end he deserves.

222
00:20:05,815 --> 00:20:08,665
And now we'll get everything we deserve.

223
00:20:09,065 --> 00:20:13,565
Yenişehir and Karacahisar and
all the lands that belong to us.

224
00:20:14,955 --> 00:20:18,985
Osman's absence will cause a civil war.

225
00:20:19,705 --> 00:20:22,645
And they can't stop it.

226
00:20:23,885 --> 00:20:27,295
An army without a
leader will end in defeat, Olof.

227
00:20:30,695 --> 00:20:32,875
And what about Ophelia?
What happened to her?

228
00:20:34,905 --> 00:20:37,435
Her body is on its way to the Emperor.

229
00:20:37,675 --> 00:20:43,105
She has wiped out like anyone who
stands against us, Kantakuzenos.

230
00:20:44,015 --> 00:20:47,165
That's cool.

231
00:20:49,135 --> 00:20:53,415
So let's shed some Turkish
blood and destroy Yenişehir.

232
00:21:06,035 --> 00:21:11,515
Watch out, Orhan! They will test you.

233
00:21:11,865 --> 00:21:13,555
They will test your strength.

234
00:21:14,455 --> 00:21:18,225
Don't worry, mother! I have held many
councils with the masters of Karacahisar.

235
00:21:18,255 --> 00:21:19,705
And I know how to
manage it.

236
00:21:19,705 --> 00:21:25,565
There you are the master of a state, but
here you will sit at the head of the state.

237
00:21:26,275 --> 00:21:29,165
Your father's shadow
overshadows their bravery there.

238
00:21:31,195 --> 00:21:35,715
Those who are against Osman will try to
make you obey them.

239
00:21:36,385 --> 00:21:39,605
They will show themselves as affected
by your father's absence.

240
00:21:39,655 --> 00:21:44,255
They will appear concerned and
have good intentions but...

241
00:21:45,445 --> 00:21:48,885
There will be those among them who
do not wish Osman Bey to come back.

242
00:21:50,975 --> 00:21:55,735
There are many enemies but are
there any enemies in the court, mother?

243
00:21:57,015 --> 00:22:04,045
Orhan, everyone is fighting to fill the
void when the center of power is absent.

244
00:22:12,605 --> 00:22:15,875
Power makes everyone
compete for it, including the good people.

245
00:22:22,135 --> 00:22:24,205
Don't ever worry, mother.

246
00:22:27,115 --> 00:22:29,765
We will discipline these souls
that struggle for power.

247
00:22:29,935 --> 00:22:32,755
May Allah protect us from falling
into the whims of power.

248
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:36,075
Our job is to spread justice.

249
00:22:49,105 --> 00:22:50,925
We are on standby.

250
00:22:50,985 --> 00:22:55,175
Even if they oppose me, I will
oppose them all.

251
00:22:57,325 --> 00:22:59,405
Inshallah, my son.

252
00:23:00,345 --> 00:23:04,345
You look so well, and being the head of
the Court will also look good on you.

253
00:23:05,465 --> 00:23:08,325
Inshallah, my mother!

254
00:23:08,445 --> 00:23:09,835
Amin.

255
00:23:10,445 --> 00:23:13,965
If we are going to establish
a state, it is thanks to the mothers.

256
00:23:14,425 --> 00:23:15,785
May Allah bless you.

257
00:23:46,915 --> 00:23:49,105
My Bey.

258
00:23:49,125 --> 00:23:50,505
Kumral Abdal.

259
00:23:53,075 --> 00:23:54,255
Kumral Abdal.

260
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:57,775
We are here.

261
00:24:07,905 --> 00:24:10,305
Sir, the other exit to the mine is safe.

262
00:24:10,355 --> 00:24:11,935
- We have to hurry.
- Yes.

263
00:24:14,565 --> 00:24:15,695
Osman Bey.

264
00:24:15,825 --> 00:24:17,375
Thank Allah.

265
00:24:17,955 --> 00:24:19,695
Hey, hey!

266
00:24:21,085 --> 00:24:22,435
My Bey.

267
00:24:23,475 --> 00:24:24,795
Come on.

268
00:24:28,465 --> 00:24:30,565
My Bey.

269
00:24:31,695 --> 00:24:33,255
Thank Allah.

270
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:36,595
Thank Allah who brought us together.

271
00:24:39,535 --> 00:24:40,845
Come on.

272
00:24:59,205 --> 00:25:00,525
Blood.

273
00:25:04,145 --> 00:25:05,665
There are traces of blood.

274
00:25:05,695 --> 00:25:07,785
Alps, take precautions.

275
00:25:09,165 --> 00:25:10,695
This way.

276
00:25:10,755 --> 00:25:12,075
Come on.

277
00:25:16,865 --> 00:25:18,385
My Osman.

278
00:25:22,845 --> 00:25:24,215
Hang on.

279
00:25:24,285 --> 00:25:25,845
Hang on, my brothers.

280
00:25:25,955 --> 00:25:29,025
Hang on, my brothers.

281
00:25:29,325 --> 00:25:30,355
Hang on.

282
00:25:34,945 --> 00:25:36,365
Brothers, are you all right?

283
00:25:36,445 --> 00:25:38,725
Hang on, my brothers.

284
00:25:40,005 --> 00:25:41,595
Collect firewood.

285
00:25:41,705 --> 00:25:43,235
Set fires.

286
00:25:43,285 --> 00:25:44,345
No, no.

287
00:25:44,395 --> 00:25:46,605
We can't light fires, they may
know where we are.

288
00:25:46,615 --> 00:25:48,385
- Boran.
- My Bey.

289
00:25:54,445 --> 00:25:55,805
My Bey.

290
00:25:56,035 --> 00:25:57,405
Hang on.

291
00:26:03,345 --> 00:26:05,105
Bite hard.

292
00:26:17,605 --> 00:26:19,185
Thanks.

293
00:26:27,685 --> 00:26:29,205
Alps.

294
00:26:36,035 --> 00:26:37,875
- Bala.
- Osman.

295
00:26:38,515 --> 00:26:40,525
Be careful, Alps.

296
00:26:40,605 --> 00:26:41,905
My Osman.

297
00:26:41,905 --> 00:26:43,405
My Bala.

298
00:26:44,365 --> 00:26:45,945
My Bala.

299
00:26:48,045 --> 00:26:49,815
You are fine, right?.

300
00:26:49,825 --> 00:26:51,685
I'm fine, I'm fine

301
00:26:51,685 --> 00:26:54,225
Alps? How are they, are they okay?

302
00:26:54,305 --> 00:26:55,885
They are also fine.

303
00:27:01,985 --> 00:27:03,735
Thank Allah we survived.

304
00:27:03,735 --> 00:27:05,315
They will get better.

305
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:08,195
Bala.

306
00:27:08,215 --> 00:27:10,215
We have to tell Malhun...

307
00:27:10,525 --> 00:27:12,395
to increase the measures.

308
00:27:13,485 --> 00:27:15,225
That dog, Olof...

309
00:27:15,375 --> 00:27:17,895
His target will now be Yenişehir.

310
00:27:18,165 --> 00:27:21,745
Before we came, Malhun appointed
Orhan as your agent.

311
00:27:21,875 --> 00:27:24,085
Aktemur increased the number of Alps.

312
00:27:24,125 --> 00:27:25,885
We have taken precautions beforehand.

313
00:27:25,885 --> 00:27:28,225
Good, good what you did.

314
00:27:28,605 --> 00:27:30,105
But it is not enough.

315
00:27:30,625 --> 00:27:32,685
And now we're going to send her a letter.

316
00:27:33,055 --> 00:27:36,085
They will protect the city
as if preparing for a big war.

317
00:27:36,145 --> 00:27:37,465
Letter?

318
00:27:37,535 --> 00:27:39,325
Why don't we go to them?

319
00:27:39,325 --> 00:27:41,335
Shall we make the enemy rejoice, my Bey?

320
00:27:41,345 --> 00:27:45,205
We will cheer them up
until they get drunk with joy.

321
00:27:48,755 --> 00:27:51,795
My Bey, you say the enemy is at our gates.

322
00:27:51,825 --> 00:27:53,825
Our children and our families.

323
00:27:54,125 --> 00:27:56,665
Where are we going now
if we're not going to them?

324
00:28:00,285 --> 00:28:01,875
To Marmaracık.

325
00:28:05,295 --> 00:28:07,145
We're going to Marmaracık.

326
00:28:11,985 --> 00:28:15,025
They went crazy in Osman's
palace a long time ago.

327
00:28:15,485 --> 00:28:19,185
And his two wives are trying to
get back on their feet in his absence.

328
00:28:19,665 --> 00:28:21,935
Malhun has taken over the reins.

329
00:28:22,235 --> 00:28:24,275
As for Bala, she went to the cave.

330
00:28:24,365 --> 00:28:27,165
To find the bones of her beloved husband.

331
00:28:29,055 --> 00:28:30,615
Osman is dead.

332
00:28:31,565 --> 00:28:33,305
And they will die too.

333
00:28:33,935 --> 00:28:38,195
And the whole Yenişehir will be
affected by our black curse.

334
00:28:38,885 --> 00:28:41,465
You'd better not speak
so confidently, Olof.

335
00:28:43,185 --> 00:28:45,725
You know, Osman is a demon.

336
00:28:45,775 --> 00:28:48,565
Not as much as us, Kantakuzenos.

337
00:28:49,405 --> 00:28:51,935
If Osman had escaped from that cave...

338
00:28:52,525 --> 00:28:55,955
would dear Malhun have been so troubled?

339
00:28:55,955 --> 00:29:00,515
You have to learn to take
Frigg's word, Kantakuzenos.

340
00:29:02,965 --> 00:29:05,005
Malhun panicked so much that she...

341
00:29:05,305 --> 00:29:07,695
Orhan to replace Osman.

342
00:29:07,775 --> 00:29:11,345
Poor Orhan, you should have
seen the fear in his eyes.

343
00:29:11,345 --> 00:29:12,735
Nice.

344
00:29:13,215 --> 00:29:15,795
That fear will bring them to their knees.

345
00:29:18,355 --> 00:29:22,205
We will make this land on which our
blood has spilled a hell for them.

346
00:29:23,775 --> 00:29:26,325
But we need more than this, Frigg.

347
00:29:27,165 --> 00:29:28,915
You will know everything.

348
00:29:28,915 --> 00:29:30,915
How many soldiers do they have?

349
00:29:30,915 --> 00:29:32,225
How many archers?

350
00:29:32,225 --> 00:29:35,445
You'll learn the number of
soldiers at each door.

351
00:29:36,095 --> 00:29:38,195
I'll come up with more, my love.

352
00:29:38,575 --> 00:29:41,085
I'll even know the breath in their lungs.

353
00:29:44,225 --> 00:29:45,765
...but for now...

354
00:29:48,285 --> 00:29:49,815
If you excuse me.

355
00:29:55,615 --> 00:29:57,385
First Yenişehir.

356
00:29:58,005 --> 00:30:00,845
And then we shall have the
Byzantine throne, Olof.

357
00:30:02,435 --> 00:30:05,215
The army of Byzantium
will be under your command.

358
00:30:05,455 --> 00:30:09,025
And your name will be remembered
with the brave warriors for ages.

359
00:30:14,895 --> 00:30:19,405
First, let's hang Orhan's
head on Yenişehir.

360
00:30:20,815 --> 00:30:23,875
Now the dog Olof knows I died in the cave.

361
00:30:23,915 --> 00:30:26,505
He thinks I'm under the ground.

362
00:30:26,525 --> 00:30:30,445
We'll take Marmaracık like never expected.

363
00:30:31,745 --> 00:30:35,135
And since he thinks you're dead, he'll
take all his men to Yenişehir.

364
00:30:35,135 --> 00:30:38,085
Exactly, it will leave Marmaracık empty.

365
00:30:38,485 --> 00:30:40,515
We will take advantage of that void.

366
00:30:41,005 --> 00:30:42,385
Now?

367
00:30:42,405 --> 00:30:43,985
The Alps are wounded.

368
00:30:44,005 --> 00:30:45,885
How are we going now?

369
00:30:45,905 --> 00:30:47,775
Alps will go to the tribe.

370
00:30:47,785 --> 00:30:49,105
Cerkutay.

371
00:30:49,185 --> 00:30:50,555
My Bey.

372
00:30:51,235 --> 00:30:54,575
Go with the Alps to the
tribe and treat them.

373
00:30:54,575 --> 00:30:57,155
But secretly, don't let anyone see you.

374
00:30:57,295 --> 00:31:00,335
Your command, my Bey.
Come on, my brothers, come on.

375
00:31:00,335 --> 00:31:02,335
Since we're hunting Olof...

376
00:31:02,965 --> 00:31:05,025
we should explore.

377
00:31:05,285 --> 00:31:09,295
Let's go to Marmaracık, which
will belong to us.

378
00:31:11,935 --> 00:31:13,315
Let's go, Osman Bey.

379
00:31:14,965 --> 00:31:16,285
Come on.

380
00:31:17,165 --> 00:31:18,745
Come on, Alps.

381
00:31:26,475 --> 00:31:29,345
Yenişehir

382
00:31:33,485 --> 00:31:36,045
Where is Osman Bey?
Has anyone seen it?

383
00:31:36,315 --> 00:31:40,705
Alps came out all of a
sudden, that's what we heard.

384
00:31:41,105 --> 00:31:44,145
Is it possible to leave this
position to a child of this age?

385
00:31:45,050 --> 00:31:46,550
Beys.

386
00:31:48,040 --> 00:31:49,550
Calm down.

387
00:31:51,540 --> 00:31:54,400
And do not speak without knowledge.

388
00:31:55,740 --> 00:31:57,550
And do not eat your brother's flesh.

389
00:31:57,550 --> 00:31:59,550
They don't say anything, Öktem Bey.

390
00:31:59,550 --> 00:32:01,130
They don't say anything.

391
00:32:01,830 --> 00:32:03,110
However...

392
00:32:04,660 --> 00:32:05,760
They want to know too.

393
00:32:06,590 --> 00:32:09,040
But they don't know what
they're talking about.

394
00:32:09,460 --> 00:32:11,430
Let them control their tongues.

395
00:32:11,430 --> 00:32:14,040
So that we don't have to
teach them the limits.

396
00:32:23,330 --> 00:32:24,640
Salam Alaikum.

397
00:32:24,640 --> 00:32:27,050
Alaikum Salam.

398
00:32:57,830 --> 00:32:59,010
Attention.

399
00:33:10,050 --> 00:33:11,170
Go ahead.

400
00:33:19,540 --> 00:33:25,040
With the ninety-nine
names of Allah, the court opens.

401
00:33:27,250 --> 00:33:32,000
In the name of Allah the Merciful.

402
00:33:33,670 --> 00:33:35,700
May I, Orhan Bey?

403
00:33:37,940 --> 00:33:39,960
What happened, Orhan Bey?

404
00:33:40,990 --> 00:33:42,790
Is it true what we heard?

405
00:33:43,840 --> 00:33:45,930
What did you hear, Bayındır Bey?

406
00:33:46,160 --> 00:33:48,030
How is Osman Bey?

407
00:33:48,480 --> 00:33:50,570
I hope his health is fine.

408
00:33:57,910 --> 00:34:01,210
Osman Bey is out to
solve a very important matter.

409
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:07,150
He left to me the Head of the Court as his representative, in my capacity as the Bey of Karacahisar.

410
00:34:09,350 --> 00:34:13,600
Osman Bey went out to conquer many times.

411
00:34:13,870 --> 00:34:18,100
He is a great Bey who does not say
what he does or what he thinks.

412
00:34:18,670 --> 00:34:24,300
This is the first time we see that he
appointed his son in his absence.

413
00:34:24,880 --> 00:34:29,500
It is clear that his return
this time is difficult.

414
00:35:04,910 --> 00:35:07,480
You're thinking of Orhan Bey, aren't you?

415
00:35:08,170 --> 00:35:10,680
I know he will do his job perfectly.

416
00:35:11,450 --> 00:35:17,340
Those who want to take advantage of
Osman's absence will be taught the lesson.

417
00:35:24,020 --> 00:35:27,780
It is our right to know as Beys...

418
00:35:28,480 --> 00:35:31,520
We want to take our positions
according to the situation.

419
00:35:33,730 --> 00:35:35,590
Isn't it, Beys?

420
00:35:35,650 --> 00:35:36,870
Yes.

421
00:35:39,350 --> 00:35:40,870
Bayındır Bey.

422
00:35:42,750 --> 00:35:44,530
A Bey's business is secret.

423
00:35:58,340 --> 00:36:00,420
I will share this secret with you.

424
00:36:03,290 --> 00:36:04,810
But it's heavy.

425
00:36:10,110 --> 00:36:13,170
Either I keep you in jail until
the campaign is over...

426
00:36:16,270 --> 00:36:18,340
Or I have to chop off your heads.

427
00:36:40,320 --> 00:36:42,340
Now tell me, Beys.

428
00:36:43,250 --> 00:36:45,280
Do you still want to listen?

429
00:36:46,160 --> 00:36:47,980
Yes, Orhan Bey.

430
00:36:52,300 --> 00:36:54,920
- Well, Orhan Bey.
- He says it's a secret.

431
00:36:55,030 --> 00:36:58,560
Don't you hear what our Bey says,
Demirhan Bey? He says it's a secret.

432
00:36:58,810 --> 00:37:01,840
We must hear the Bey's words.

433
00:37:14,210 --> 00:37:17,930
If your questions are over, I want to
hear about the other problems now.

434
00:37:18,690 --> 00:37:21,100
Yenişehir
Osman Bey's Palace

435
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:25,520
We wanted to ask about Osman Bey
and he said lots of things.

436
00:37:26,750 --> 00:37:30,240
That is what would happen if
the work was left to a young boy.

437
00:37:30,260 --> 00:37:32,960
This is not good.

438
00:37:37,400 --> 00:37:38,970
Beys.

439
00:37:42,300 --> 00:37:44,370
Orhan Bey asked...

440
00:37:44,700 --> 00:37:46,770
and you told him your problems...

441
00:37:46,770 --> 00:37:48,770
and then the court ended.

442
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:51,160
What do you want next, Beys?

443
00:37:54,950 --> 00:37:58,000
When did it become wrong to
ask about Osman Bey?

444
00:37:58,240 --> 00:38:00,750
Didn't Orhan Bey' answer
convince you, Uraz Bey?

445
00:38:00,910 --> 00:38:02,630
If you think so...

446
00:38:02,630 --> 00:38:05,200
you will wait for Osman Bey in prison.

447
00:38:05,270 --> 00:38:07,850
Isn't what you say shameful, Turgut Bey?

448
00:38:07,900 --> 00:38:10,920
If you want to see the fault, look
at each other's faces.

449
00:38:14,460 --> 00:38:16,320
No need to talk yet.

450
00:38:16,640 --> 00:38:18,660
The Court is over.

451
00:38:19,010 --> 00:38:20,730
Mind your business.

452
00:38:29,205 --> 00:38:31,245
They're planning something again.

453
00:38:32,095 --> 00:38:34,945
It will appear soon, whatever.

454
00:38:40,745 --> 00:38:43,025
If you accept...

455
00:38:43,485 --> 00:38:47,825
I want to share with you the business
that I am going to do in Marmaracık.

456
00:38:48,345 --> 00:38:49,665
Thank you.

457
00:38:49,975 --> 00:38:52,185
However...

458
00:38:52,605 --> 00:38:56,625
While there are a lot of
dealers around, why me?

459
00:38:58,245 --> 00:39:01,285
Because you are the most
skilled trader in this city.

460
00:39:01,755 --> 00:39:04,815
And the richest, Bayındır Bey.

461
00:39:05,515 --> 00:39:07,745
Aren't you in charge of everything here?

462
00:39:08,415 --> 00:39:10,005
Yes...

463
00:39:10,685 --> 00:39:12,495
Let's say I'm awake.

464
00:39:13,705 --> 00:39:15,465
Don't be afraid.

465
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:19,305
For example, Osman Bey...

466
00:39:19,885 --> 00:39:21,925
They say he's not around.

467
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:25,505
I'm sure no one else knows
the truth about it.

468
00:39:26,965 --> 00:39:28,345
Hatun.

469
00:39:30,195 --> 00:39:32,905
You are overrating me.

470
00:39:34,065 --> 00:39:39,305
I only know what everyone else knows.

471
00:39:40,635 --> 00:39:44,175
Orhan sits on the chair
in place of Osman Bey.

472
00:39:44,485 --> 00:39:47,265
And Alps are on guard everywhere.

473
00:39:48,415 --> 00:39:49,945
May Allah forbid.

474
00:39:51,165 --> 00:39:54,725
I hope nothing bad happened to Osman Bey.

475
00:39:54,865 --> 00:39:58,865
No, I hope you're wrong.

476
00:40:00,305 --> 00:40:02,735
I don't even want to
think about Osman Bey's death.

477
00:40:02,735 --> 00:40:04,255
No.

478
00:40:04,335 --> 00:40:05,915
I do not want that.

479
00:40:05,945 --> 00:40:07,305
Who wants?

480
00:40:07,335 --> 00:40:11,225
May Allah keep Osman Bey above our heads.

481
00:40:11,775 --> 00:40:13,145
However...

482
00:40:13,485 --> 00:40:16,525
This is what it looks like, what
can we say?

483
00:40:17,145 --> 00:40:24,645
I pray to Allah to grant Orhan Bey
strength and power, Inshallah.

484
00:40:27,295 --> 00:40:29,745
While the surroundings are
complicated...

485
00:40:29,795 --> 00:40:32,925
the best we can do is trade, Bayındır Bey.

486
00:40:33,435 --> 00:40:35,655
It is not clear what
will happen to the city.

487
00:40:35,705 --> 00:40:37,595
We must increase our profits.

488
00:40:37,655 --> 00:40:40,695
Let's increase it.

489
00:40:40,995 --> 00:40:43,715
But let's talk about terms first.

490
00:40:45,955 --> 00:40:47,515
The goods your responsibility.

491
00:40:48,195 --> 00:40:49,995
Finding clients is my responsibility.

492
00:40:50,645 --> 00:40:53,365
And our profits will be equal.

493
00:40:59,265 --> 00:41:01,365
I want two-thirds.

494
00:41:08,945 --> 00:41:11,035
This is not the time to bargain.

495
00:41:13,105 --> 00:41:15,595
I accept, we agreed.

496
00:41:15,595 --> 00:41:18,295
Wait for word from me, Bayındır Bey.

497
00:41:18,905 --> 00:41:20,445
Good.

498
00:41:42,685 --> 00:41:44,225
Show up.

499
00:42:05,965 --> 00:42:08,355
Tell me, what is the
situation in Marmaracık?

500
00:42:08,355 --> 00:42:10,375
They got most of the soldiers out, my Bey.

501
00:42:10,375 --> 00:42:12,095
The castle is available for attack.

502
00:42:12,215 --> 00:42:15,395
But things are never good, my Bey.

503
00:42:15,555 --> 00:42:18,115
They captured our brother Torahan.

504
00:42:20,055 --> 00:42:21,895
Dogs.

505
00:42:22,945 --> 00:42:25,165
They will all get their punishment.

506
00:42:25,415 --> 00:42:27,915
I will cut their flesh off their bodies.

507
00:42:30,335 --> 00:42:34,605
They got those soldiers out
to attack Yenişehir.

508
00:42:35,635 --> 00:42:37,525
And we will take Marmaracık.

509
00:42:37,695 --> 00:42:39,435
And we will save Torahan.

510
00:42:39,495 --> 00:42:42,245
Wherever we had to spy, we
made that place home, my Bey.

511
00:42:42,455 --> 00:42:44,525
What is our job in conquest?

512
00:42:44,565 --> 00:42:46,585
First, you will close the horse stables.

513
00:42:46,645 --> 00:42:48,695
They can't escape anywhere.

514
00:42:48,695 --> 00:42:52,235
And when we go inside, you
will kill the archers on the walls.

515
00:42:52,365 --> 00:42:56,875
When we pull our bows,
we will not leave any of them alive.

516
00:42:57,035 --> 00:42:58,585
May Allah bless you.

517
00:42:58,765 --> 00:43:00,575
Now go to your work.

518
00:43:00,635 --> 00:43:03,785
But know the place of
the prison very well.

519
00:43:04,005 --> 00:43:05,725
We'll take Torahan first.

520
00:43:05,725 --> 00:43:07,315
We've known him
for a while, my Bey.

521
00:43:07,315 --> 00:43:09,125
It's a map of the castle.

522
00:43:14,155 --> 00:43:15,655
Oh my!

523
00:43:16,135 --> 00:43:18,135
May Allah bless my valiants.

524
00:43:18,745 --> 00:43:20,315
Come on, then.

525
00:43:20,725 --> 00:43:22,405
May our conquest be blessed.

526
00:43:22,495 --> 00:43:24,365
Thank you, my Bey.

527
00:43:28,455 --> 00:43:30,525
Where are we going
now, my dear Osman?

528
00:43:30,625 --> 00:43:32,675
To the place where it all began.

529
00:43:34,295 --> 00:43:35,825
To our tribe.

530
00:43:37,995 --> 00:43:39,305
Come on.

531
00:43:46,215 --> 00:43:47,585
Come on.

532
00:43:52,925 --> 00:43:57,735
The trade of Marmaracık will benefit
you and our city, Bayındır Bey.

533
00:43:58,395 --> 00:43:59,905
We allow you.

534
00:44:00,415 --> 00:44:02,205
This is the permission document.

535
00:44:03,455 --> 00:44:06,275
We don't ask for one thing for ourselves.

536
00:44:06,445 --> 00:44:10,635
All our money and possessions are
sacrificed for the sake of Osman Bey.

537
00:44:11,185 --> 00:44:14,555
This trade will please you, Malhun Hatun.

538
00:44:14,555 --> 00:44:17,365
Inshallah, Bayındır Bey.

539
00:44:17,565 --> 00:44:20,405
Come on, Allah bless you.

540
00:44:20,735 --> 00:44:22,305
Take care.

541
00:44:32,395 --> 00:44:33,725
My Bey.

542
00:44:34,825 --> 00:44:38,625
Do you hear the sound
of gold coins, Hüseyin?

543
00:44:39,555 --> 00:44:41,645
How can I not hear, my Bey_

544
00:44:44,315 --> 00:44:46,835
Did you know anything
about Osman Bey?

545
00:44:46,855 --> 00:44:48,655
It is said that Osman Bey
went out at night.

546
00:44:48,685 --> 00:44:50,955
And he never came back again.

547
00:44:52,185 --> 00:44:54,185
Osman is not around.

548
00:44:54,335 --> 00:44:56,215
And Orhan holds the court

549
00:44:56,915 --> 00:44:59,655
Obviously, they know something, however...

550
00:45:00,285 --> 00:45:02,005
They hide it from us.

551
00:45:02,885 --> 00:45:04,925
Something crosses my mind, however...

552
00:45:05,085 --> 00:45:06,525
What if he is dead, my Bey?

553
00:45:06,545 --> 00:45:08,335
Don't say that.

554
00:45:08,925 --> 00:45:11,645
I worked so hard to get him to like me.

555
00:45:11,745 --> 00:45:14,075
All my efforts are in vain.

556
00:45:14,855 --> 00:45:16,095
You know...

557
00:45:16,365 --> 00:45:19,775
Maybe his absence makes
us win a lot of coins, right?

558
00:45:25,145 --> 00:45:26,945
Come on, you go.

559
00:45:27,865 --> 00:45:31,385
And write a letter to Sencer Bey
telling him everything that happened.

560
00:45:31,385 --> 00:45:32,585
Your command, my Bey.

561
00:45:32,585 --> 00:45:35,175
Then prepare Marta's goods.

562
00:45:35,175 --> 00:45:37,765
We'll set off early tomorrow morning.

563
00:45:38,055 --> 00:45:39,815
Your command.

564
00:45:39,875 --> 00:45:41,585
Of course, come on.

565
00:45:56,115 --> 00:45:58,675
So, you don't feel anything
for me, do you?

566
00:46:00,425 --> 00:46:02,505
So, say this to my face.

567
00:46:14,975 --> 00:46:16,565
Subasi

568
00:46:16,645 --> 00:46:18,155
Alçiçek.

569
00:46:21,865 --> 00:46:23,445
Do you want something?

570
00:46:23,455 --> 00:46:24,835
We'll talk.

571
00:46:25,065 --> 00:46:27,105
There is nothing to talk about.

572
00:46:27,125 --> 00:46:29,015
Get away from my table.

573
00:46:29,095 --> 00:46:31,605
I said we'll talk, Alçiçek Hatun.

574
00:46:32,725 --> 00:46:34,105
Alone

575
00:46:39,075 --> 00:46:41,625
Shall I not get rid of you, Subasi?

576
00:46:55,015 --> 00:46:58,285
What are you seeking, Subasi?

577
00:47:16,655 --> 00:47:18,245
Say what you're going to say.

578
00:47:18,245 --> 00:47:20,055
I don't have much time.

579
00:47:26,775 --> 00:47:28,575
I'll ask a question and go.

580
00:47:29,875 --> 00:47:31,965
I heard some things last night.

581
00:47:34,695 --> 00:47:38,755
But my ears and heart can't believe it.

582
00:47:41,085 --> 00:47:43,675
What you heard is true, Subasi.

583
00:47:48,295 --> 00:47:53,735
So, say it again as you
look me in the eye.

584
00:47:56,155 --> 00:47:58,015
Heads up, Alçiçek.

585
00:48:01,275 --> 00:48:03,795
Do you want your heart broken, Subasi?

586
00:48:05,275 --> 00:48:06,985
Does it matter for you?

587
00:48:12,715 --> 00:48:14,295
Alçiçek.

588
00:48:17,505 --> 00:48:19,825
I loved you.

589
00:48:26,695 --> 00:48:28,575
Do you love me too?

590
00:48:34,015 --> 00:48:35,245
No.

591
00:48:49,915 --> 00:48:52,485
You misunderstood me, Subasi.

592
00:48:52,845 --> 00:48:54,885
If I am the reason for this...

593
00:48:55,375 --> 00:48:56,895
sorry.

594
00:49:00,335 --> 00:49:02,035
Take these too.

595
00:49:04,095 --> 00:49:05,925
If my mother had not come...

596
00:49:06,455 --> 00:49:08,295
I wouldn't have taken it.

597
00:49:11,615 --> 00:49:13,665
I bought these two earrings for you.

598
00:49:16,105 --> 00:49:18,135
If they don't matter to you....

599
00:49:19,185 --> 00:49:20,515
throw them away.

600
00:49:32,985 --> 00:49:34,375
I...

601
00:49:38,525 --> 00:49:40,075
I was wrong.

602
00:49:40,945 --> 00:49:42,515
Excuse me.

603
00:49:44,065 --> 00:49:47,115
I won't bother you again and I
won't get in your way.

604
00:49:55,305 --> 00:49:57,175
Take your dagger, too.

605
00:50:00,465 --> 00:50:02,325
Never hurt anyone again.

606
00:50:09,715 --> 00:50:12,225
Aktemur.

607
00:50:15,605 --> 00:50:17,845
You loved the wrong person, however...

608
00:50:18,375 --> 00:50:20,155
you got the answer.

609
00:50:32,415 --> 00:50:34,305
Don't, Alçiçek.

610
00:50:35,015 --> 00:50:36,525
Don't.

611
00:50:53,395 --> 00:50:57,985
Hurr up, Bayındır.

612
00:50:58,675 --> 00:51:01,985
Otherwise, Osman's
nephew will not calm down.

613
00:52:03,235 --> 00:52:06,255
Our tent, which was the
home of our big dreams...

614
00:52:07,535 --> 00:52:09,235
Bala.

615
00:52:24,205 --> 00:52:25,955
Thank Allah.

616
00:52:26,185 --> 00:52:29,155
It was our privilege to see
those dreams come true, my Bey.

617
00:52:38,885 --> 00:52:42,615
We have planted the seeds
of state in this tribe.

618
00:52:43,255 --> 00:52:47,595
May Allah make you among
His righteous servants.

619
00:52:47,635 --> 00:52:49,635
Amin.

620
00:52:54,055 --> 00:52:56,635
In the name of Allah the Merciful.

621
00:52:57,935 --> 00:53:02,805
You are the ones who will
carry the banner of Allah.

622
00:53:03,405 --> 00:53:06,135
Move your horses forward.

623
00:53:07,155 --> 00:53:11,235
Now, we take care of the it and
make it grow in Yenişehir.

624
00:53:12,705 --> 00:53:17,035
I pray to Allah that He swears for us to
see it as a tree and harvest its fruits.

625
00:53:25,455 --> 00:53:27,685
Amin, my dear Osman.

626
00:54:03,335 --> 00:54:05,545
On the one hand, they
considered you invaders.

627
00:54:05,555 --> 00:54:07,885
On the other hand, you rest,

628
00:54:09,885 --> 00:54:12,315
Do not be jealous of
your brothers, Cerkutay.

629
00:54:12,705 --> 00:54:13,885
Turgut Bey.

630
00:54:15,335 --> 00:54:16,855
I've done all of that work.

631
00:54:17,635 --> 00:54:21,085
And no one came and
called me Ghazi Cerkutay.

632
00:54:23,855 --> 00:54:25,155
Brother.

633
00:54:27,165 --> 00:54:32,665
Didn't you rest all this time because
you weren't hearing?

634
00:54:32,785 --> 00:54:34,285
Yes.

635
00:54:34,615 --> 00:54:36,365
I did.

636
00:54:36,435 --> 00:54:39,505
I ate and drank a lot.

637
00:54:41,955 --> 00:54:44,535
You will not like the
food of the tribe anymore.

638
00:54:46,555 --> 00:54:49,135
You're used to
Ülgen Hatun's food, aren't you?

639
00:54:49,585 --> 00:54:50,935
Now...

640
00:54:52,605 --> 00:54:56,185
In fact, she is a skilled woman.

641
00:55:00,355 --> 00:55:01,935
Cerguday.

642
00:55:17,135 --> 00:55:22,355
It's like she's taking revenge
on me for the times I didn't hear.

643
00:55:25,085 --> 00:55:28,435
I can hear her voice even
though she's not here.

644
00:55:30,135 --> 00:55:31,635
Oh.

645
00:55:32,505 --> 00:55:34,605
Really, Cerkutay?

646
00:55:34,935 --> 00:55:38,485
Do you hear Ülgen Hatun's voice now?

647
00:55:42,285 --> 00:55:44,835
Cerguday, come on!

648
00:55:46,505 --> 00:55:48,355
Do you still hear it?

649
00:55:51,855 --> 00:55:53,155
I hear it.

650
00:55:56,185 --> 00:55:58,055
She is calling me

651
00:56:00,235 --> 00:56:02,505
Please, brother, do not fear us.

652
00:56:03,555 --> 00:56:05,105
Cerkutay.

653
00:56:05,535 --> 00:56:07,655
You're basically a Ghazi.

654
00:56:07,925 --> 00:56:09,845
And it didn't stop
at hearing the voice.

655
00:56:09,885 --> 00:56:11,885
I smell.

656
00:56:12,905 --> 00:56:15,055
I smell her food.

657
00:56:16,635 --> 00:56:18,185
The smell of bulghur.

658
00:56:18,735 --> 00:56:19,715
My Allah.

659
00:56:19,715 --> 00:56:21,715
Don't worry, my dear Cerkutay.

660
00:56:21,765 --> 00:56:24,885
We also hear Ülgen Hatun's voice.

661
00:56:25,205 --> 00:56:30,235
But smelling that food is only your skill.

662
00:56:36,025 --> 00:56:39,475
Are you deceiving me?

663
00:56:39,585 --> 00:56:41,585
Allah forgive you.

664
00:56:41,715 --> 00:56:44,165
Allah forgive you.

665
00:56:44,885 --> 00:56:47,205
Come on, run, don't make the bulghur wai.t

666
00:56:47,205 --> 00:56:48,345
Come on.

667
00:56:48,415 --> 00:56:50,115
Go eat your food.

668
00:56:54,935 --> 00:56:57,435
Eat it all.

669
00:57:12,385 --> 00:57:13,935
Cerguday.

670
00:57:19,885 --> 00:57:24,005
Thank you, I was very hungry, Ülgen Hatun.

671
00:57:26,585 --> 00:57:30,445
But I still don't hear.

672
00:57:30,465 --> 00:57:32,465
What? How?

673
00:57:33,105 --> 00:57:35,435
Do not you hear?

674
00:57:36,105 --> 00:57:37,905
I came on foot.

675
00:57:38,965 --> 00:57:40,515
He doesn't hear.

676
00:57:40,545 --> 00:57:42,095
Anyway.

677
00:57:42,335 --> 00:57:44,335
Eat, Cerguday, eat.

678
00:57:51,705 --> 00:57:53,035
Enjoy it.

679
00:57:54,005 --> 00:58:01,155
Don't worry, don't worry, I'll find
a way to heal your ears.

680
00:58:04,505 --> 00:58:06,335
They said there was a herb.

681
00:58:06,515 --> 00:58:08,015
There is a herb.

682
00:58:08,985 --> 00:58:10,285
Enjoy it.

683
00:58:10,705 --> 00:58:13,855
There is a herb.

684
00:58:16,285 --> 00:58:17,615
I found it.

685
00:58:18,075 --> 00:58:24,125
Did you understand? I will
find it and heal your ears.

686
00:58:26,105 --> 00:58:27,885
What am I doing?

687
00:58:29,835 --> 00:58:32,535
You eat, Cerguday, eat bread too.

688
00:58:32,535 --> 00:58:35,085
The food is very tasty.

689
00:58:36,485 --> 00:58:38,335
- Enjoy it.
- Thank you.

690
00:58:43,855 --> 00:58:45,935
What do you say? I do not hear you!

691
00:58:45,975 --> 00:58:47,725
I don't hear, I don't hear!

692
00:58:47,755 --> 00:58:49,755
Right?

693
00:58:51,065 --> 00:58:52,385
Good.

694
00:59:15,755 --> 00:59:17,285
Ülgen Hatun.

695
00:59:18,305 --> 00:59:20,055
What are you doing?

696
00:59:20,515 --> 00:59:22,365
I'm leaving, eat your food.

697
00:59:48,785 --> 00:59:50,355
In the name of Allah.

698
00:59:51,355 --> 00:59:52,935
In the name of Allah.

699
00:59:53,625 --> 00:59:55,465
Thank you, may Allah bless
your hands, Ülgen Hatun.

700
00:59:55,495 --> 00:59:56,865
Enjoy it.

701
00:59:56,905 --> 00:59:58,905
Enjoy it, brother.

702
00:59:59,445 --> 01:00:01,205
I hope you'll leave us food.

703
01:00:01,225 --> 01:00:03,745
Come, brother, there is
enough food for all of us.

704
01:00:13,335 --> 01:00:15,135
I no longer hear.

705
01:00:17,145 --> 01:00:18,645
I do not hear.

706
01:00:26,605 --> 01:00:28,155
I do not hear.

707
01:00:37,205 --> 01:00:39,955
Cerguday will leave for us, right?

708
01:00:52,935 --> 01:00:55,435
Osman Bey summons you.

709
01:01:01,705 --> 01:01:03,455
We must not keep my Bey waiting.

710
01:01:03,455 --> 01:01:05,955
Marmaracık Castle)

711
01:01:09,640 --> 01:01:11,370
Yenişehir

712
01:01:12,090 --> 01:01:14,620
It is smashed by our enemies.

713
01:01:15,970 --> 01:01:18,450
But tomorrow, it will all
be over for the Turks.

714
01:01:18,480 --> 01:01:20,480
We will take back our lands.

715
01:01:21,200 --> 01:01:22,770
Explain, Frigg.

716
01:01:25,940 --> 01:01:29,440
They are increasing the security
in Yenişehir, they are very worried.

717
01:01:29,730 --> 01:01:31,450
Some soldiers came out.

718
01:01:33,300 --> 01:01:35,270
They're obviously looking for Osman.

719
01:01:35,430 --> 01:01:37,130
Let them search.

720
01:01:37,430 --> 01:01:39,430
It will be difficult for them to find him

721
01:01:44,250 --> 01:01:46,250
Continue, Frigg.

722
01:01:49,230 --> 01:01:52,420
The largest door is the west door and
most units will be there.

723
01:01:53,230 --> 01:01:56,050
And I'll clean that door
for Olof and his men.

724
01:01:58,000 --> 01:02:02,880
The number of soldiers is not
enough to eliminate these units, my love.

725
01:02:04,850 --> 01:02:10,180
For this reason, I will have my
men sneak into the castle all day.

726
01:02:12,050 --> 01:02:15,200
They will be there for
you to clean the door.

727
01:02:17,850 --> 01:02:21,850
But I will make the main
attack from the east.

728
01:02:25,050 --> 01:02:28,590
When their soldiers head west...

729
01:02:29,050 --> 01:02:31,550
I will enter through the eastern door...

730
01:02:32,450 --> 01:02:36,300
and I will crush all who come before me.

731
01:02:43,580 --> 01:02:45,330
You will crush them, my love.

732
01:02:45,450 --> 01:02:49,080
I'll scatter the men
who snuck in all over town.

733
01:02:50,950 --> 01:02:53,080
And when the massacre
begins in the city...

734
01:02:53,080 --> 01:02:56,730
The eastern door will
open completely for you.

735
01:02:58,300 --> 01:03:00,330
They still think I'm their friend.

736
01:03:00,450 --> 01:03:03,430
For this reason, I will take on
the most important mission.

737
01:03:04,800 --> 01:03:07,300
I will enter the mansion with 20 soldiers.

738
01:03:08,050 --> 01:03:12,100
You'll have entered the city while
they get busy with me.

739
01:03:12,480 --> 01:03:16,550
And I'll be in front of Osman's family
when they find out about the massacre.

740
01:03:17,530 --> 01:03:20,830
First, I will tell them to their faces
that the war has begun...

741
01:03:23,150 --> 01:03:25,430
...then I will cut their throats.

742
01:03:25,430 --> 01:03:28,250
And I will take care of the women
in the mansion.

743
01:03:32,000 --> 01:03:36,480
I will cut off their gentle hands
that prepare delicious meals.

744
01:03:38,900 --> 01:03:43,030
I will turn that mansion into a barn for
our beautiful horses.

745
01:03:43,180 --> 01:03:49,650
But first, in order to make it defenseless,
I have to drag Malhun into my trap.

746
01:03:50,500 --> 01:03:52,600
I will handle her outside.

747
01:03:54,400 --> 01:03:57,200
Tomorrow, before sunset,
Yenisehir will be ours.

748
01:03:57,200 --> 01:03:58,980
Only Yenisehir?

749
01:03:58,980 --> 01:04:00,250
No.

750
01:04:00,250 --> 01:04:02,250
The Turks killed the Cardinal.

751
01:04:02,880 --> 01:04:05,700
So Vatican will give me a huge army.

752
01:04:07,250 --> 01:04:09,750
I will take the emperor's throne first.

753
01:04:09,880 --> 01:04:12,480
And then I will take back
our lands from the Turks

754
01:04:14,550 --> 01:04:16,400
The army will be yours, Olof..

755
01:04:16,500 --> 01:04:18,200
And that's why I'm here.

756
01:04:18,750 --> 01:04:22,780
I will let my ravens eat all the Turks!

757
01:04:23,200 --> 01:04:26,050
I will bring death to them all.

758
01:04:26,050 --> 01:04:28,050
Yenisehir will be ours.

759
01:04:31,730 --> 01:04:32,980
Ours.

760
01:04:34,800 --> 01:04:36,580
It will be ours.

761
01:04:41,700 --> 01:04:43,280
We'll conquer Marmaracik.

762
01:04:44,180 --> 01:04:46,280
We will be quick and ruthless.

763
01:04:46,950 --> 01:04:49,000
There mustn't even be a single mistake.

764
01:04:51,600 --> 01:04:54,400
We'll go in and take it.

765
01:04:55,180 --> 01:04:58,200
That place is now more than
just a property to us.

766
01:05:01,430 --> 01:05:02,780
Turahan is imprisoned there.

767
01:05:03,130 --> 01:05:05,430
We'll get him out of there safe and sound.

768
01:05:05,430 --> 01:05:07,430
With his goods, inshallah.

769
01:05:10,630 --> 01:05:12,150
Here it is.

770
01:05:16,430 --> 01:05:18,950
The dungeon that Samil told us about.

771
01:05:19,080 --> 01:05:20,950
Just below the castle hall.

772
01:05:22,100 --> 01:05:26,600
While we eliminate the soldiers, a team
of Alps will enter the dungeon.

773
01:05:26,700 --> 01:05:28,500
We will not waste time.

774
01:05:28,850 --> 01:05:30,150
My Bey.

775
01:05:30,600 --> 01:05:32,680
The siege of the castle can last for days.

776
01:05:34,050 --> 01:05:36,050
Can we come in, my Bey?

777
01:05:36,450 --> 01:05:37,750
Come!

778
01:05:44,780 --> 01:05:46,300
Peace be upon you.

779
01:05:46,300 --> 01:05:47,850
And may peace be upon you.

780
01:05:47,850 --> 01:05:49,850
What do you do here?

781
01:05:50,980 --> 01:05:54,300
My Bey, don't keep us away from the fight.

782
01:05:57,600 --> 01:06:02,930
My Bey, a Ghazi's wound
is healed in another fight.

783
01:06:03,750 --> 01:06:05,530
We will come too.

784
01:06:09,600 --> 01:06:11,450
Fair enough.

785
01:06:14,580 --> 01:06:17,450
However, conquering the castle
will not last for days.

786
01:06:19,050 --> 01:06:24,600
We will ruin their homes and take them
without any alp being harmed.

787
01:06:27,230 --> 01:06:34,300
Now, they will want to sneak into Yenişehir
while we're away.

788
01:06:36,830 --> 01:06:40,700
First, they will attack and
they will be successful.

789
01:06:44,480 --> 01:06:47,980
But it would never occur to them
that we would take Marmaracik.

790
01:06:48,580 --> 01:06:50,080
The enemy is on alert.

791
01:06:51,580 --> 01:06:53,840
We are not going to sleep tonight, sons!

792
01:06:54,080 --> 01:06:56,350
Are the streets under control, Subasi?

793
01:06:57,200 --> 01:06:59,730
I put an Alp on every street in Yenisehir.

794
01:07:00,230 --> 01:07:01,600
Insufficient.

795
01:07:01,600 --> 01:07:03,430
We don't know the
men power of the enemy.

796
01:07:03,430 --> 01:07:05,930
Put three alps instead of one.

797
01:07:07,780 --> 01:07:10,330
Mother, this is our home.

798
01:07:10,330 --> 01:07:12,130
We should outnumber them.

799
01:07:12,550 --> 01:07:14,280
I know, son.

800
01:07:14,300 --> 01:07:17,800
I know, but Yenisehir is entrusted to us.

801
01:07:18,250 --> 01:07:21,250
We cannot feel safe
just because its our land.

802
01:07:22,400 --> 01:07:26,800
I will send messengers to Karacahisar.
My alps will be here in the morning.

803
01:07:26,800 --> 01:07:30,280
I have placed archers on the roofs and
we have alps in each building...

804
01:07:30,280 --> 01:07:32,930
...as they may attack at anytime.

805
01:07:33,150 --> 01:07:35,200
This is not enough.

806
01:07:35,200 --> 01:07:39,450
If we can't handle them outside,
we will draw back to our buildings.

807
01:07:40,180 --> 01:07:43,230
Our narrow alleys will absorb their
advantage in number.

808
01:07:43,230 --> 01:07:45,550
If necessary, we will withdraw
to the mansion.

809
01:07:47,150 --> 01:07:49,880
We will destroy them one by one.

810
01:07:52,700 --> 01:07:55,980
Kutlu Alp, tell the alps and dervishes.

811
01:07:56,200 --> 01:07:58,250
No one will insist on fighting.

812
01:07:58,250 --> 01:08:00,750
If necessary, they will retreat and
withdraw to the mansion.

813
01:08:01,030 --> 01:08:02,600
Yes my Bey.

814
01:08:04,550 --> 01:08:10,480
Send messengers to Inegol, Karacahisar,
Bilecik. Ask for reinforcement.

815
01:08:10,480 --> 01:08:12,480
As you command, Malhun Hatun.

816
01:08:22,930 --> 01:08:24,800
Yenisehir is entrusted to us.

817
01:08:25,779 --> 01:08:27,600
We will take care of it, my Bey.

818
01:08:31,600 --> 01:08:33,149
However...

819
01:08:35,080 --> 01:08:37,580
The owner of this...

820
01:08:45,080 --> 01:08:46,950
How are you now, Osman Bey?

821
01:08:52,185 --> 01:08:54,705
I moved the alps from
Inegol to Yenisehir.

822
01:08:55,075 --> 01:08:58,465
Yet I don't know if our forces
are sufficient, Osman Bey.

823
01:08:58,944 --> 01:09:01,295
We will take our strength from the tribe.

824
01:09:01,785 --> 01:09:03,785
We will attack with the alps in the tribe.

825
01:09:03,825 --> 01:09:06,125
Will they be sufficient
for a siege, my Bey?

826
01:09:06,175 --> 01:09:08,245
There is not going to be a siege.

827
01:09:09,185 --> 01:09:14,234
The fortress will ask for provisions
from Bayindir Bey.

828
01:09:14,305 --> 01:09:17,395
Malhun Hatun approved him.

829
01:09:18,665 --> 01:09:21,685
We'll escort those three carriages.

830
01:09:22,165 --> 01:09:24,545
They will be waiting for provisions.

831
01:09:24,725 --> 01:09:29,765
When they open the gates
they will see us in front of them.

832
01:09:30,765 --> 01:09:33,564
What about the security
of Yenisehir, my Bey?

833
01:09:33,745 --> 01:09:35,795
Malhun Hatun will handle it.

834
01:09:36,005 --> 01:09:41,524
Alps and dervishes will be in disguise
and guard the town.

835
01:09:42,255 --> 01:09:46,274
But they will not stop them from
entering Yenisehir.

836
01:09:46,484 --> 01:09:49,295
They will proceed to the center.

837
01:09:51,635 --> 01:09:56,915
Olof and those with him
will march towards our trap.

838
01:09:57,185 --> 01:10:00,785
We will attack them when the time comes.

839
01:10:03,225 --> 01:10:05,505
First Marmarcik.

840
01:10:05,935 --> 01:10:11,605
And then the whole world.

841
01:10:12,975 --> 01:10:14,985
Oktem Tribe

842
01:10:17,545 --> 01:10:18,895
Thank you.

843
01:10:19,765 --> 01:10:21,325
Enjoy it.

844
01:10:24,795 --> 01:10:26,525
Thank you, daughter.

845
01:10:34,285 --> 01:10:43,295
Our Bey let the child sit on the throne
and who knows what adventure he's into!

846
01:10:45,345 --> 01:10:48,515
Orhan Bey said what he had to say.

847
01:10:48,915 --> 01:10:51,415
What are you questioning here, Bayindir?

848
01:10:51,595 --> 01:10:54,915
What am I questioning here?

849
01:10:55,735 --> 01:11:02,415
Whenever this man disappears from sight,
he comes back with a thousand troubles!

850
01:11:05,215 --> 01:11:09,755
Who knows what kind of
trouble he'll cause now!

851
01:11:10,065 --> 01:11:13,355
The last time he went to Constantinople...

852
01:11:13,685 --> 01:11:14,935
...Batur Alp...

853
01:11:15,155 --> 01:11:16,855
Bayindir!

854
01:11:17,555 --> 01:11:20,885
Why do you keep bringing up
what's already over?

855
01:11:21,035 --> 01:11:23,225
What is already over, Oktem Bey?

856
01:11:23,445 --> 01:11:26,005
Bayindir Bey is right.

857
01:11:27,585 --> 01:11:33,465
Hatun, even if it is still not over yet...

858
01:11:33,715 --> 01:11:37,945
Osman Bey will give us the opportunity
to take revenge.

859
01:11:43,405 --> 01:11:47,365
Marmaragic is about to be conquered.

860
01:11:47,945 --> 01:11:51,875
It's that dog Olof's home!

861
01:11:53,155 --> 01:11:55,955
I trust him completely.

862
01:11:57,205 --> 01:12:00,625
Osman Bey will conquer Marmaracik.

863
01:12:00,625 --> 01:12:02,785
And he will make it a home for the Turks!

864
01:12:02,785 --> 01:12:05,555
We are not asking you not to trust.

865
01:12:05,775 --> 01:12:09,155
We only ask you to be on alert.

866
01:12:10,255 --> 01:12:15,765
Imagine what a man, who deceives
even the emperor, would do to you!

867
01:12:15,985 --> 01:12:19,125
Don't you agree with me, Bengi Hatun?

868
01:12:19,425 --> 01:12:21,775
It doesn't matter, Bayindir Bey.

869
01:12:22,045 --> 01:12:25,555
Oktem Bey has become arrogant.

870
01:12:25,735 --> 01:12:29,395
He trusts Osman Bey more than
he trusts you and me.

871
01:12:30,125 --> 01:12:32,105
Stop this.

872
01:12:32,435 --> 01:12:37,655
We trusted Osman Bey at the door of death.
He protected us at that time.

873
01:12:39,905 --> 01:12:41,555
Don't worry about me.

874
01:12:41,705 --> 01:12:45,485
Why are you angry, Oktem Bey?

875
01:12:46,645 --> 01:12:50,085
If that man trusts you so much...

876
01:12:50,355 --> 01:12:54,475
Why does he not disclose his location?
Why is he hiding it from you?

877
01:12:55,385 --> 01:13:00,905
It's no use to trust someone
if they don't trust you back!

878
01:13:02,615 --> 01:13:04,635
Time will show...

879
01:13:04,825 --> 01:13:09,495
If I'm right about trusting Osman Bey,
or wrong like you say.

880
01:13:12,395 --> 01:13:15,925
Good night, Bayindir.

881
01:13:22,115 --> 01:13:25,495
Subasi is around Alcicek again.

882
01:13:25,745 --> 01:13:27,935
Be careful.

883
01:13:30,495 --> 01:13:32,905
Good night.

884
01:13:44,055 --> 01:13:46,735
What is he saying, Bengi Hatun?

885
01:13:47,745 --> 01:13:51,765
Nothing important,
it was about the stalls.

886
01:13:51,765 --> 01:13:52,905
Good

887
01:13:58,715 --> 01:14:01,295
Oh Alcicek!

888
01:14:01,855 --> 01:14:05,605
I know what I will do to you.

889
01:14:14,385 --> 01:14:20,655
Aktemur, son of Gunduz Bey,
who terrorized seven countries.

890
01:14:21,235 --> 01:14:25,845
I shudder as I look into your eyes.

891
01:14:26,145 --> 01:14:29,985
- I will make him talk!
- Alcicek!

892
01:14:30,625 --> 01:14:33,005
You need to control your anger, Alcicek?

893
01:14:33,185 --> 01:14:34,735
Are you well?

894
01:14:34,925 --> 01:14:40,285
If I had a thousand necks, I'd sacrifice them
all to stop the tears dropping off your eyes.

895
01:14:40,435 --> 01:14:45,135
If only that dagger had stabbed my heart
so I wouldn't have heard all these!

896
01:14:45,525 --> 01:14:47,605
Alcicek Hatun.

897
01:14:56,985 --> 01:15:00,305
This is enough.

898
01:15:04,575 --> 01:15:06,335
Aktemur?

899
01:15:12,225 --> 01:15:14,735
Come in, mother.

900
01:15:42,640 --> 01:15:50,730
I fed my little boy Aydogdu
and put him to sleep, how is my big son?

901
01:15:54,320 --> 01:16:01,910
Tell me, Aktemur,
which mountain are you on top of this time?

902
01:16:05,750 --> 01:16:10,740
I'm under the ground, mother.
Don't worry about me.

903
01:16:11,440 --> 01:16:15,560
How can a mother not worry about her son?

904
01:16:15,990 --> 01:16:18,880
Do you think motherhood ends
when the boys grow up?

905
01:16:19,220 --> 01:16:28,770
The tears you shed inside you, my son,
burn my heart.

906
01:16:32,960 --> 01:16:38,660
Your heart has no reason to hurt, mother.
Relieve.

907
01:16:42,650 --> 01:16:44,200
Son.

908
01:16:45,970 --> 01:16:51,980
I have no one but you and your brother.

909
01:16:52,280 --> 01:16:55,060
That's why I got mad at that girl.

910
01:16:55,970 --> 01:16:59,960
- If she hurts my son...
- It's over, mother!

911
01:17:00,390 --> 01:17:02,240
It's over now!

912
01:17:04,110 --> 01:17:06,970
Alcicek thing is over.

913
01:17:13,280 --> 01:17:15,600
She doesn't love me.

914
01:17:18,000 --> 01:17:21,870
It's over.
Don't worry.

915
01:17:26,990 --> 01:17:32,360
I hope for your best, son.
For the best.

916
01:17:43,480 --> 01:17:46,500
I stabbed him.

917
01:17:46,710 --> 01:17:49,610
But I am the one whose heart hurts.

918
01:17:50,670 --> 01:17:53,540
Love issues are too hard.

919
01:17:54,560 --> 01:17:56,110
Are you in love?

920
01:17:57,740 --> 01:18:00,830
If you fell in love,
then why did you reject the man?

921
01:18:01,000 --> 01:18:02,570
To test him.

922
01:18:04,790 --> 01:18:06,920
And what do you mean by that,
Alcicek Hatun?

923
01:18:09,740 --> 01:18:11,780
What if his feelings are not true?

924
01:18:12,980 --> 01:18:15,240
What if its just a whim?

925
01:18:17,740 --> 01:18:19,800
I must know first.

926
01:18:19,940 --> 01:18:21,680
Does he really love me?

927
01:18:21,790 --> 01:18:23,810
He must make me believe his love first.

928
01:18:24,600 --> 01:18:27,110
So that I set off on this difficult way
with him.

929
01:18:27,285 --> 01:18:28,995
Alcicek!

930
01:18:35,185 --> 01:18:37,755
I told you not to meet that man.

931
01:18:38,315 --> 01:18:42,855
You're in my tent and
describe the love you have for him?

932
01:18:42,875 --> 01:18:44,235
Mother, I'm...

933
01:18:44,295 --> 01:18:47,455
Will you let people gossip
about our family?

934
01:18:47,695 --> 01:18:49,515
I won't allow it, Alcicek.

935
01:18:49,755 --> 01:18:53,295
You are not going to see even his shade.

936
01:18:53,445 --> 01:18:54,975
It's enough, mother!

937
01:18:55,055 --> 01:18:57,055
Enough, what do you want from me?

938
01:18:57,495 --> 01:18:59,365
Why are you pressing me like that?

939
01:18:59,435 --> 01:19:01,195
Why are you so angry?

940
01:19:01,605 --> 01:19:03,665
What wrong did Subasi do?

941
01:19:03,715 --> 01:19:06,955
Isn't it wrong to hover around
you without my permission?

942
01:19:08,445 --> 01:19:11,105
But I will also hold him
accountable for this immoral act.

943
01:19:12,095 --> 01:19:13,205
How shameless!

944
01:19:13,485 --> 01:19:15,925
Despite all my words,
he's still chasing you!

945
01:19:16,085 --> 01:19:17,435
Mother!

946
01:19:17,465 --> 01:19:19,525
Let your ears hear
what your mouth says!

947
01:19:19,685 --> 01:19:21,185
Watch your words!

948
01:19:21,205 --> 01:19:23,635
What immoral act
have you seen from Aktemur?

949
01:19:23,635 --> 01:19:25,095
Pull yourself together!

950
01:19:28,195 --> 01:19:31,475
You disobey your mother for the man
you met recently.

951
01:19:32,175 --> 01:19:33,765
- Mother...
- Shut it!

952
01:19:33,835 --> 01:19:36,445
Alcicek, shut it.

953
01:19:37,955 --> 01:19:41,115
You will never see that young man again.

954
01:19:42,025 --> 01:19:45,135
If he encounters you on the way,
you will change your path.

955
01:20:07,185 --> 01:20:08,695
Kayi's men!

956
01:20:10,275 --> 01:20:12,305
We will enter into a difficult battle!

957
01:20:14,425 --> 01:20:16,685
Even if we don't walk to the enemy...

958
01:20:17,795 --> 01:20:20,465
They will keep coming towards us.

959
01:20:22,765 --> 01:20:26,095
This is a fight between right and wrong.

960
01:20:28,835 --> 01:20:30,455
My strong-hearted alps!

961
01:20:33,385 --> 01:20:38,285
Now it is time to strike the home of enemy
like a steel flail!

962
01:20:39,145 --> 01:20:40,715
Marmaracik is a place which...

963
01:20:41,145 --> 01:20:44,705
...reaches to the land of the enemy
like a hammer.

964
01:20:46,275 --> 01:20:48,285
If we claim that fortress...

965
01:20:48,855 --> 01:20:51,395
Many more conquers
will be available for us!

966
01:20:52,125 --> 01:20:53,995
Our horses are facing forward

967
01:20:54,005 --> 01:20:56,375
Our faces are always facing west

968
01:20:56,925 --> 01:20:58,675
Come on Alps!

969
01:20:59,835 --> 01:21:01,725
It's time to conquer!

970
01:21:34,350 --> 01:21:36,560
Tell me Subasi, what's the situation?

971
01:21:36,570 --> 01:21:39,280
We have sent messengers to all our lands,
they are preparing alps.

972
01:21:39,680 --> 01:21:42,470
And I brought the alps from
Karacahisar to Yenisehir.

973
01:21:42,910 --> 01:21:44,750
They are all waiting for
your orders, Mother.

974
01:21:46,860 --> 01:21:48,510
What are the conditions around?

975
01:21:48,510 --> 01:21:50,480
Did you take precautions around the town?

976
01:21:50,480 --> 01:21:54,600
Our spies are walking around dressed as
shepherds and merchants, Malhun Hatun.

977
01:21:59,810 --> 01:22:01,130
Ayse.

978
01:22:01,140 --> 01:22:02,930
Any news on Marta?

979
01:22:03,050 --> 01:22:05,940
The woman is like an ant.
She doesn't rest.

980
01:22:06,090 --> 01:22:08,620
She is always working.

981
01:22:09,030 --> 01:22:11,820
We'll see if she is a hardworking ant...

982
01:22:12,300 --> 01:22:14,360
Or a snake who is waiting to bite.

983
01:22:15,085 --> 01:22:16,675
Soldiers!

984
01:22:16,765 --> 01:22:19,055
Today we will smear Yenişehir with blood!

985
01:22:19,685 --> 01:22:21,945
We will end Turks...

986
01:22:22,955 --> 01:22:24,995
...who shed our blood!

987
01:22:26,045 --> 01:22:27,615
Soldiers!

988
01:22:28,215 --> 01:22:31,715
Odin's table is for warriors!

989
01:22:33,225 --> 01:22:34,785
Deserve Valhalla!

990
01:22:35,265 --> 01:22:37,045
We will not pity on...

991
01:22:38,165 --> 01:22:40,515
...anyone who shed our blood...

992
01:22:41,565 --> 01:22:43,255
...anyone who damaged Byzantine!

993
01:22:43,255 --> 01:22:46,725
We will kill everyone who gets in our way!

994
01:22:46,885 --> 01:22:52,125
Kill! Kill! Kill!

995
01:22:52,155 --> 01:22:54,685
Kill! Kill! Kill!

996
01:22:57,235 --> 01:22:59,095
You will infiltrate into Yenisehir.

997
01:23:00,235 --> 01:23:01,535
Remember!

998
01:23:02,265 --> 01:23:05,015
The easiest way to eliminate the enemy...

999
01:23:05,505 --> 01:23:07,245
...is to damage it inside.

1000
01:23:07,955 --> 01:23:11,685
Some of you will die on this way.

1001
01:23:12,845 --> 01:23:15,655
Remove fear from your hearts!

1002
01:23:17,645 --> 01:23:20,415
Deserve the table of Odin!

1003
01:23:21,765 --> 01:23:23,625
And when the signal comes to you...

1004
01:23:23,915 --> 01:23:25,485
You will start the war.

1005
01:23:25,875 --> 01:23:27,925
To spread the black curse!

1006
01:23:29,105 --> 01:23:34,605
Black curse! Black curse!

1007
01:23:34,765 --> 01:23:41,335
Black curse! Black curse!

1008
01:24:17,085 --> 01:24:19,155
Bey, they are coming

1009
01:24:19,905 --> 01:24:22,475
Let them come, let them come.

1010
01:24:25,565 --> 01:24:27,305
- Boran.
- My Bey.

1011
01:24:27,725 --> 01:24:29,525
- Get ready.
- Yes my Bey.

1012
01:24:53,995 --> 01:24:55,825
Has the gold been discovered, Huseyin?

1013
01:24:55,875 --> 01:24:57,665
Impossible, my Bey.

1014
01:25:07,855 --> 01:25:09,675
Put your weapons
back in their sheaths!

1015
01:25:13,355 --> 01:25:16,415
We go to Marmaracik to trade
so that the Turkmens can get rich

1016
01:25:17,435 --> 01:25:20,015
What sin have I done?
Why do you cross my road?

1017
01:25:20,105 --> 01:25:22,645
Your sins are between you and Allah,
Bayindir Bey.

1018
01:25:23,145 --> 01:25:24,865
You are what we need.

1019
01:25:27,165 --> 01:25:28,965
What's it, Turgut Bey?

1020
01:25:29,335 --> 01:25:31,205
For the Good's sake.

1021
01:25:31,245 --> 01:25:32,945
Watch who is coming.

1022
01:25:38,825 --> 01:25:40,365
Osman Bey.

1023
01:25:43,035 --> 01:25:44,535
Bayindir Bey.

1024
01:25:48,765 --> 01:25:50,605
You will take us to Karacahisar.

1025
01:25:51,055 --> 01:25:53,615
I give you my money, my possessions,
and my soul, Osman Bey.

1026
01:25:54,205 --> 01:25:55,955
But what is your plan?

1027
01:25:55,995 --> 01:25:58,535
Marmaracik is going to be
Turks' from now on.

1028
01:25:59,445 --> 01:26:01,535
You used to say that you love to fight.

1029
01:26:01,555 --> 01:26:03,315
Now is the time.

1030
01:26:03,385 --> 01:26:04,975
You will come with us.

1031
01:26:12,735 --> 01:26:17,825
What a shame it would be not to join you
on a holy fight, Osman Bey! Eyvallah!

1032
01:26:24,622 --> 01:26:26,222
Eyvallah.

1033
01:26:31,540 --> 01:26:35,110
Yenişehir without Osman is like
a warrior without armor, Olof.

1034
01:26:35,510 --> 01:26:37,870
I am going to visit my friends now.

1035
01:26:37,900 --> 01:26:39,490
Orhan Bey.

1036
01:26:39,570 --> 01:26:41,350
On his little shoulders...

1037
01:26:41,380 --> 01:26:43,920
...Yenisehir's huge responsibility.
How misfortune for him.

1038
01:26:44,100 --> 01:26:45,630
Go, Kantakouzanos.

1039
01:26:46,320 --> 01:26:48,090
Our friendship with them...

1040
01:26:48,520 --> 01:26:50,300
...is our biggest weapon.

1041
01:26:50,330 --> 01:26:52,910
It'll be last time
they see my friendly face.

1042
01:26:52,990 --> 01:26:55,130
And the first time they'll see
my enemy face.

1043
01:26:55,130 --> 01:26:56,800
I will gouge out their eyes.

1044
01:26:57,510 --> 01:26:59,360
I will fill fire in them.

1045
01:27:00,760 --> 01:27:02,620
Neither Orhan nor Malhun.

1046
01:27:03,650 --> 01:27:05,480
None of them will breathe.

1047
01:27:06,590 --> 01:27:08,720
I will not let anyone breathe in Yenisehir.

1048
01:27:10,490 --> 01:27:12,380
At the end of the war...

1049
01:27:12,540 --> 01:27:17,750
I will have taken my revenge,
you will have taken the gift you deserve.

1050
01:27:18,180 --> 01:27:19,680
The crown of Byzantine!

1051
01:27:20,580 --> 01:27:22,040
They have nowhere to run.

1052
01:27:22,790 --> 01:27:25,540
We will avenge and I will wear that crown!

1053
01:27:26,440 --> 01:27:28,020
We will attack from all four sides.

1054
01:27:28,550 --> 01:27:29,880
Let's go.

1055
01:27:31,270 --> 01:27:32,580
Let's go.

1056
01:27:58,390 --> 01:27:59,940
Come on, let's get started.

1057
01:28:00,630 --> 01:28:03,790
We will smear Yenişehir
with the black curse!

1058
01:28:04,500 --> 01:28:05,810
Go!

1059
01:28:09,985 --> 01:28:11,690
Oktem Tribe.

1060
01:28:17,685 --> 01:28:20,215
There is no news from Osman Bey yet.

1061
01:28:21,485 --> 01:28:23,985
What does he hide again?

1062
01:28:26,835 --> 01:28:29,875
Allah knows what calamity he will cause us

1063
01:28:32,345 --> 01:28:34,435
But you know this is your fault.

1064
01:28:35,695 --> 01:28:37,745
That man does whatever he wants to you.

1065
01:28:38,265 --> 01:28:40,315
Then he gives a speech
about fight and war.

1066
01:28:40,665 --> 01:28:43,205
- And you believe...
- What should I have done, Hatun?

1067
01:28:43,815 --> 01:28:46,365
What could we do when we stood with him

1068
01:28:46,705 --> 01:28:49,215
Osman Bey is getting stronger day by day.

1069
01:28:50,415 --> 01:28:52,235
We will get stronger too.

1070
01:28:53,455 --> 01:28:56,005
You won't be strong and grow bigger
waiting here like this.

1071
01:28:56,825 --> 01:28:57,825
Look at Osman!

1072
01:28:58,035 --> 01:29:01,535
He secretly solves all his business
without even taking a single breath!

1073
01:29:01,535 --> 01:29:03,385
It is not a time to stay idle.

1074
01:29:03,475 --> 01:29:05,535
We are not going to
stay idle either, Hatun.

1075
01:29:05,625 --> 01:29:10,195
Is Osman making a deal with
the infidels secretly hiding from you?

1076
01:29:12,455 --> 01:29:15,985
What he did before troubled us.

1077
01:29:16,715 --> 01:29:20,575
Let's see to whom
he will bring trouble now.

1078
01:29:24,725 --> 01:29:29,435
I will travel to Yenisehir, go to the
mansion and see if Hatuns know anything.

1079
01:29:30,095 --> 01:29:31,395
Don't worry.

1080
01:29:31,675 --> 01:29:33,535
I'll know what's going on.

1081
01:29:33,695 --> 01:29:35,565
I'll act as if I'm looking for you.

1082
01:29:36,275 --> 01:29:38,275
Don't leave the tribe today.

1083
01:29:40,185 --> 01:29:42,685
- Hatun!
- Don't worry Oktem Bey.

1084
01:29:43,475 --> 01:29:44,775
I will find out.

1085
01:29:44,955 --> 01:29:46,835
There is no other way.

1086
01:30:00,665 --> 01:30:02,495
What's wrong with Alcicek?

1087
01:30:03,665 --> 01:30:05,165
Nothing.

1088
01:30:06,495 --> 01:30:08,565
I solved it, don't worry.

1089
01:30:31,185 --> 01:30:32,685
Open the gates.

1090
01:31:39,655 --> 01:31:41,475
Only you can enter.

1091
01:31:43,775 --> 01:31:45,515
Is this reasonable?

1092
01:31:45,835 --> 01:31:47,395
What do you mean by that?

1093
01:31:48,495 --> 01:31:50,565
Will I carry all these goods myself?

1094
01:31:51,885 --> 01:31:53,725
- Huseyin!
- My Bey!

1095
01:31:54,585 --> 01:31:56,725
I changed my mind.
We are leaving!

1096
01:31:58,965 --> 01:32:00,545
Merchant!

1097
01:32:00,725 --> 01:32:02,815
You have just arrived,
where are you going?

1098
01:32:04,805 --> 01:32:07,085
What does it mean that you don't
let my men in?

1099
01:32:07,085 --> 01:32:08,685
We need only you.

1100
01:32:09,265 --> 01:32:10,765
Soldiers!

1101
01:32:10,855 --> 01:32:12,395
Search the wagons!

1102
01:32:12,655 --> 01:32:14,485
Turn it upside down!

1103
01:32:16,155 --> 01:32:18,895
We don't receive free goods everyday.

1104
01:32:33,255 --> 01:32:35,345
It's a trap! Soldiers, attack!

1105
01:32:38,835 --> 01:32:40,335
You are not getting any goods!

1106
01:32:40,375 --> 01:32:42,405
Karacahisar is ours from now on!

1107
01:32:42,585 --> 01:32:44,595
Samil! Aykut!

1108
01:32:49,945 --> 01:32:51,245
O Right!

1109
01:32:51,895 --> 01:32:53,595
Come on alps!

1110
01:32:53,985 --> 01:32:55,485
Allah is the greatest!

1111
01:34:02,905 --> 01:34:04,205
Attack them!

1112
01:34:11,725 --> 01:34:13,285
Turgut!

1113
01:34:15,625 --> 01:34:17,185
Samil, come on!

1114
01:34:18,945 --> 01:34:20,645
Don't resist, commander!

1115
01:34:20,705 --> 01:34:21,705
Don't resist.

1116
01:34:21,725 --> 01:34:23,815
Protecting Karacahisar Castle
is my mission!

1117
01:34:23,905 --> 01:34:27,475
I will fight you
until my last breath!

1118
01:34:31,625 --> 01:34:33,355
Are you all right, Commander?

1119
01:34:33,405 --> 01:34:35,425
What are you doing here?
Go fight!

1120
01:34:40,165 --> 01:34:41,955
I spilled my blood!

1121
01:34:42,265 --> 01:34:45,095
And I will cut your man
to pieces in front of you, Osman!

1122
01:34:47,355 --> 01:34:51,245
Inform Olof with a pigeon at once!
Osman is here! Run!

1123
01:35:00,145 --> 01:35:02,935
They're holding Turahan
at the end of the corridor, my Bey.

1124
01:35:02,935 --> 01:35:04,695
We didn't come here in vain, brother.

1125
01:35:04,745 --> 01:35:06,215
Of course we will get him out.

1126
01:35:23,405 --> 01:35:25,195
Are you okay brothers?

1127
01:35:25,205 --> 01:35:27,055
We are fine, thank Allah.

1128
01:35:27,965 --> 01:35:31,695
We will save our brother and make this
fortress a graveyard for them!

1129
01:35:32,115 --> 01:35:33,615
Come on then!

1130
01:35:47,505 --> 01:35:48,805
Let's go!

1131
01:35:50,175 --> 01:35:51,475
Let's go!

1132
01:35:54,375 --> 01:35:57,405
I showed you respect when
you came to Constantinople.

1133
01:35:57,645 --> 01:36:00,495
But Olof was right, you are not a friend.

1134
01:36:00,745 --> 01:36:03,185
You are not a friend.
You are the greatest enemy!

1135
01:36:07,725 --> 01:36:12,815
And you, like the Emperor,
do not know who is friend and who is foe!

1136
01:36:12,915 --> 01:36:17,925
You cannot deceive me, Osman Bey,
I will kill you and bury you here

1137
01:36:17,925 --> 01:36:19,805
This is my land now!

1138
01:36:20,055 --> 01:36:22,075
I decide who gets buried!

1139
01:36:44,485 --> 01:36:46,025
Boran!

1140
01:36:47,925 --> 01:36:49,975
Take Commander to the prison.

1141
01:36:51,045 --> 01:36:54,285
- He has things to tell me.
- Eyvallah my Bey!

1142
01:37:35,865 --> 01:37:39,895
Your death must be close.
You lost so much blood.

1143
01:37:53,725 --> 01:37:55,715
You are my ticket.

1144
01:37:56,075 --> 01:38:00,085
And when I get out of here,
I'll feed my dogs with you!

1145
01:38:00,485 --> 01:38:01,795
Move!

1146
01:38:04,445 --> 01:38:09,645
When Kantakouzanos and Frigg open
the gates of Yenisehir, we will attack

1147
01:38:11,355 --> 01:38:13,365
You will not pity anyone

1148
01:38:15,365 --> 01:38:19,705
Whoever shows mercy will be killed by me
after the war!

1149
01:38:20,365 --> 01:38:25,565
If you come back with a clean axe,
I will paint it with your blood!

1150
01:38:27,435 --> 01:38:29,095
Have courage, brothers!

1151
01:38:29,575 --> 01:38:33,655
We will rip out the heart of Turks!

1152
01:38:35,095 --> 01:38:36,655
I don't want any mistakes!

1153
01:38:37,565 --> 01:38:41,595
Everyone who opposes us in this land...

1154
01:38:42,325 --> 01:38:43,665
...will be dead!

1155
01:38:53,405 --> 01:38:54,735
Freddy.

1156
01:39:23,625 --> 01:39:26,125
Come quickly, Olof!
Osman is not dead.

1157
01:39:26,455 --> 01:39:29,015
He has come with his men
and they are going to take the castle.

1158
01:39:29,015 --> 01:39:30,325
No!

1159
01:39:31,275 --> 01:39:32,645
no!

1160
01:39:34,505 --> 01:39:37,385
Osman! Osman!

1161
01:39:37,835 --> 01:39:40,205
I don't know how you got out of that hole!

1162
01:39:40,795 --> 01:39:43,015
But Marmaracik will be your grave.

1163
01:39:46,135 --> 01:39:47,685
Olof.

1164
01:39:48,125 --> 01:39:49,825
What do we do now?

1165
01:39:49,825 --> 01:39:51,125
No!

1166
01:39:51,785 --> 01:39:54,105
Tell Frig right away!

1167
01:39:55,275 --> 01:39:59,285
They have to raid Yenisehir without us.

1168
01:39:59,765 --> 01:40:01,155
Let's go!

1169
01:40:01,165 --> 01:40:04,215
We are going to Marmaracik at once!

1170
01:40:04,615 --> 01:40:07,675
And we'll walk around holding
Osman's head!

1171
01:40:08,005 --> 01:40:11,095
Come on! Come on!

1172
01:40:25,385 --> 01:40:27,885
Turahan, my brother.

1173
01:40:29,115 --> 01:40:32,665
This is not good.
Where is this Turahan, brother?

1174
01:40:34,255 --> 01:40:36,035
This way, Turgut Bey.

1175
01:40:36,045 --> 01:40:37,365
Let's go.

1176
01:40:57,205 --> 01:40:58,795
Boran!

1177
01:41:20,875 --> 01:41:22,225
Boran!

1178
01:41:22,265 --> 01:41:25,785
I didn't give up on you under the rock.
Do you think I would now?

1179
01:42:07,065 --> 01:42:08,605
My Bala.

1180
01:43:24,855 --> 01:43:26,435
Thank Allah.

1181
01:43:27,435 --> 01:43:29,025
Thank Allah.

1182
01:44:20,125 --> 01:44:23,405
You will die.
You lasted too long.

1183
01:44:23,845 --> 01:44:27,675
Go ahead.
Stop talking and act.

1184
01:44:39,065 --> 01:44:40,835
That dog is here.

1185
01:44:42,705 --> 01:44:44,265
We are here brother.

1186
01:44:44,305 --> 01:44:46,805
We will not leave you with the infidel!

1187
01:44:49,865 --> 01:44:51,225
Step back!

1188
01:44:53,625 --> 01:44:54,945
Step back!

1189
01:45:00,295 --> 01:45:03,415
Get out of here now, I'm out of here!

1190
01:45:05,375 --> 01:45:07,435
You can't go anywhere.

1191
01:45:08,375 --> 01:45:12,645
Even if you get out of here,
you can't control this lion.

1192
01:45:46,635 --> 01:45:48,195
Come on brother.

1193
01:45:49,255 --> 01:45:50,765
Are you fine?

1194
01:45:50,815 --> 01:45:52,605
I'm fine brother.

1195
01:46:18,505 --> 01:46:20,205
It was a nice fight.

1196
01:46:34,765 --> 01:46:36,545
If you didn't have me...

1197
01:46:37,215 --> 01:46:40,525
How would you cross
these great walls?

1198
01:46:47,935 --> 01:46:49,495
We would demolish and enter.

1199
01:46:49,585 --> 01:46:52,395
Yes, it's not something
we haven't done before.

1200
01:46:53,285 --> 01:46:55,145
We would destroy everything.

1201
01:46:55,185 --> 01:46:56,435
Yes.

1202
01:46:56,445 --> 01:46:58,685
So don't boast about yourself,
Bayindir Bey.

1203
01:46:59,755 --> 01:47:01,345
Bala Hatun.

1204
01:47:02,555 --> 01:47:07,575
Your alps underestimate my service!

1205
01:47:08,545 --> 01:47:10,385
Not at all, Bayindir Bey.

1206
01:47:10,505 --> 01:47:11,875
Thank you very much.

1207
01:47:12,225 --> 01:47:14,245
Your business has been very profitable.

1208
01:47:14,425 --> 01:47:16,005
Turks have another property now.

1209
01:47:16,045 --> 01:47:20,425
I would go up until Constantinople if
Osman Bey asked me to do so!

1210
01:47:21,605 --> 01:47:22,955
Thank you very much.

1211
01:47:29,805 --> 01:47:32,095
Bala Hatun is grateful to us.

1212
01:47:33,325 --> 01:47:37,875
We now know who we are going to approach
to get close with Osman Bey.

1213
01:47:38,135 --> 01:47:39,275
We know it now, my Bey.

1214
01:47:57,255 --> 01:47:59,375
Marmaracik is ours now.

1215
01:47:59,995 --> 01:48:01,525
Take down the flags!

1216
01:48:14,575 --> 01:48:15,965
Bala.

1217
01:48:16,145 --> 01:48:17,475
My Bey!

1218
01:48:56,555 --> 01:48:58,445
Thank you very much, my Allah.

1219
01:48:59,305 --> 01:49:00,825
Thank you very much.

1220
01:49:05,850 --> 01:49:07,740
Welcome Bengi Hatun.

1221
01:49:16,340 --> 01:49:18,410
Where's Malhun Hatun, Ulgen Hatun?

1222
01:49:21,720 --> 01:49:23,790
What's it, Bengi Hatun?

1223
01:49:29,430 --> 01:49:32,630
Yenişehir is empty.
I can't find the person I'm looking for.

1224
01:49:34,030 --> 01:49:36,100
Everyone is in their business
and occupations.

1225
01:49:36,490 --> 01:49:38,860
I'm looking for Oktem Bey,
but I can't find him

1226
01:49:39,300 --> 01:49:41,350
I heard that Osman Bey is absent as well.

1227
01:49:41,470 --> 01:49:43,870
Did they go somewhere together?
Do you know anything?

1228
01:49:45,130 --> 01:49:48,290
Bengi Hatun, I know what I should know.

1229
01:49:49,140 --> 01:49:51,170
I know where Osman Bey is.

1230
01:49:51,600 --> 01:49:56,330
However, it's not me who should know where
Oktem Bey is. It's you.

1231
01:49:58,980 --> 01:50:00,820
Do you think I know?

1232
01:50:02,970 --> 01:50:05,500
There are someone else who knows him
better than me!

1233
01:50:12,790 --> 01:50:14,100
Come in.

1234
01:50:24,040 --> 01:50:25,340
Here.

1235
01:50:34,430 --> 01:50:35,760
For you.

1236
01:50:36,510 --> 01:50:37,880
Thank you.

1237
01:50:47,420 --> 01:50:51,100
Oktem is reserved, Malhun Hatun.

1238
01:50:52,600 --> 01:50:54,410
But he is reserved only to me.

1239
01:50:55,600 --> 01:50:58,500
He doesn't tell me where
he's going or what he's doing.

1240
01:50:59,570 --> 01:51:02,070
He wasn't like this with Zuleyha.

1241
01:51:03,150 --> 01:51:08,080
He would consult her first,
he would go and tell her about it.

1242
01:51:09,850 --> 01:51:12,250
I don't understand, Bengi Hatun.
Who is Zuleyha?

1243
01:51:15,190 --> 01:51:17,020
The first wife of Oktem.

1244
01:51:18,390 --> 01:51:19,760
Zuleyha.

1245
01:51:20,640 --> 01:51:23,160
Look, I feel uncomfy even while
mentioning her name.

1246
01:51:25,040 --> 01:51:27,630
I didn't know he was married before.

1247
01:51:27,640 --> 01:51:29,150
Nobody knew it.

1248
01:51:29,940 --> 01:51:31,960
Same story, Malhun Hatun.

1249
01:51:32,070 --> 01:51:34,630
Zuleyha wasn't able to give birth.

1250
01:51:35,700 --> 01:51:37,880
She is dead and gone.

1251
01:51:39,170 --> 01:51:40,550
But...

1252
01:51:42,340 --> 01:51:45,850
Oktem's love for her never ended.

1253
01:51:48,020 --> 01:51:55,270
Every time I look inside Oktem's eyes,
I see Zuleyha.

1254
01:51:57,120 --> 01:52:00,190
But what can I do?
She is the first wife!

1255
01:52:02,080 --> 01:52:03,900
Don't think I'm bad now.

1256
01:52:04,580 --> 01:52:06,330
No, not at all.

1257
01:52:07,440 --> 01:52:09,490
The first wife is unforgettable.

1258
01:52:11,220 --> 01:52:15,280
You may think it's stupid to get jealous
of a dead person, but..

1259
01:52:16,880 --> 01:52:18,620
I'm jealous. That's it.

1260
01:52:21,490 --> 01:52:23,240
Women get jealous.

1261
01:52:26,160 --> 01:52:30,220
Aren't you jealous, Malhun Hatun?

1262
01:52:32,950 --> 01:52:37,730
Bengi Hatun, before everything,
we are a state.

1263
01:52:37,940 --> 01:52:42,160
We leave our feelings behind
when we deal with the state issues.

1264
01:52:43,040 --> 01:52:44,870
Jealousy is impotence.

1265
01:52:45,390 --> 01:52:47,890
We have no right to fall
into this heedlessness.

1266
01:52:48,890 --> 01:52:51,980
But you don't have such problems.
You don't know it.

1267
01:52:53,090 --> 01:52:56,660
So I am listening to you.
Tell me about it.

1268
01:52:57,980 --> 01:52:59,310
Thank you.

1269
01:53:00,160 --> 01:53:02,690
Not talking to anyone about this
makes me sick inside.

1270
01:53:03,450 --> 01:53:06,690
My heart could not bear it anymore,
so my tongue spoke it.

1271
01:53:07,740 --> 01:53:10,270
This issue isn't spoken with
a random person.

1272
01:53:16,320 --> 01:53:18,200
But you are not a random one.

1273
01:53:20,100 --> 01:53:21,680
You understand me.

1274
01:53:23,780 --> 01:53:27,340
I couldn't give Oktem a boy.

1275
01:53:30,150 --> 01:53:32,230
I had Batur, and he's gone too.

1276
01:53:32,560 --> 01:53:35,500
I only have Alcicek left in my tent now.

1277
01:53:36,590 --> 01:53:39,840
And I have no intention of ever losing her,
Malhun Hatun.

1278
01:53:41,640 --> 01:53:44,170
My daughter means everything to me.

1279
01:53:45,650 --> 01:53:48,200
A child is a mother's masterpiece,
Bengi Hatun.

1280
01:53:48,960 --> 01:53:50,730
Hug your daughter.

1281
01:53:51,410 --> 01:53:56,450
Digging down a ended issue
doesn't give you any good.

1282
01:53:56,620 --> 01:53:59,180
On the contrary, it damages you.

1283
01:54:00,130 --> 01:54:02,210
Don't think about it anymore.

1284
01:54:02,860 --> 01:54:07,640
It only hurts your heart.

1285
01:54:18,560 --> 01:54:20,340
Let me leave now.

1286
01:54:22,020 --> 01:54:23,910
I need to find my daughter
and my husband.

1287
01:54:24,740 --> 01:54:26,630
Of course, Bengi Hatun.

1288
01:54:45,630 --> 01:54:50,800
I have dropped the seeds of suspicion
inside you, Malhun Hatun.

1289
01:55:04,640 --> 01:55:07,440
You brave soldiers!

1290
01:55:08,010 --> 01:55:11,020
You are here to stain Yenisehir with blood

1291
01:55:32,610 --> 01:55:34,650
Listen to me very well now.

1292
01:55:35,400 --> 01:55:37,640
When Kantakouzanos gets into action...

1293
01:55:37,640 --> 01:55:41,040
We will attack the soldiers in the east
and open Olof's path.

1294
01:55:41,370 --> 01:55:42,980
You, Commanders.

1295
01:55:43,370 --> 01:55:48,630
You'll spread your soldiers all over
the city when Olof comes.

1296
01:55:50,410 --> 01:55:51,730
However....

1297
01:55:53,180 --> 01:55:55,190
...Keep your eyes on the mansion.

1298
01:55:55,900 --> 01:56:00,390
If even one person gets out, kill them.

1299
01:56:12,430 --> 01:56:14,760
We tracked everyone down
like you asked, ma'am.

1300
01:56:14,760 --> 01:56:18,260
Prince Aladdin is in the courthouse
and the others are in the mansion.

1301
01:56:21,080 --> 01:56:23,920
I will drink their blood.

1302
01:56:31,810 --> 01:56:34,690
How long do we have to wait,
Subasi Aktemur Bey?

1303
01:56:35,400 --> 01:56:37,420
.We'll let you in...

1304
01:56:38,170 --> 01:56:41,020
Whenever Malhun Hatun approves,
Kantakuzenos.

1305
01:56:41,640 --> 01:56:44,270
Impatience is not good, don't question.

1306
01:56:56,560 --> 01:57:00,070
Subasi, Malhun Hatun
is waiting for Kantakuzenos.

1307
01:57:01,830 --> 01:57:03,920
Here you go, Kantakuzenos.

1308
01:57:10,310 --> 01:57:14,860
I will stain my sword with your blood first
when Olof takes this city, Subasi.

1309
01:57:14,960 --> 01:57:17,260
You will live the same destiny
with your father.

1310
01:57:23,890 --> 01:57:25,450
Surround the shop!

1311
01:57:30,960 --> 01:57:32,260
Break the door!

1312
01:57:38,910 --> 01:57:40,480
Ayse Hatun.

1313
01:57:42,270 --> 01:57:43,860
What is going on like this?

1314
01:57:43,940 --> 01:57:47,180
Why do you lock your door
during the day, Hatun?

1315
01:57:48,580 --> 01:57:50,090
I'm scared.

1316
01:57:51,180 --> 01:57:54,260
Explosions.
There is constantly an incident in the town.

1317
01:57:55,720 --> 01:57:57,110
I locked my door.

1318
01:58:00,280 --> 01:58:03,360
Search, search everywhere.

1319
01:58:44,130 --> 01:58:46,680
There is nothing up there, Ayse Hatun.

1320
01:58:47,450 --> 01:58:50,480
Won't you say something?
What are you looking for?

1321
01:58:51,070 --> 01:58:54,590
There's a traitor, Marta.
We're looking for a trace.

1322
01:58:55,400 --> 01:58:59,290
Keep your eyes and ears open too, okay?

1323
01:59:01,520 --> 01:59:04,120
Alps, let's get out!

1324
01:59:23,590 --> 01:59:27,410
Their eyes are on us, act accordingly.

1325
02:00:21,940 --> 02:00:23,450
Malhun Hatun.

1326
02:00:23,840 --> 02:00:27,700
The best guests are the ones who
tell they're coming, Kantakouzanos.

1327
02:00:27,940 --> 02:00:29,310
Please, come.

1328
02:00:29,690 --> 02:00:31,700
Has Osman Bey not come yet?

1329
02:00:32,060 --> 02:00:34,080
Look, I brought gifts.

1330
02:00:36,770 --> 02:00:38,490
He didn't come.

1331
02:00:40,890 --> 02:00:43,960
But we got news from him.

1332
02:00:47,240 --> 02:00:48,990
What do you mean?

1333
02:00:51,850 --> 02:00:55,890
Osman Bey is in Marmaracik,
where now belongs to him.

1334
02:01:01,960 --> 02:01:03,330
I do not understand.

1335
02:01:06,470 --> 02:01:08,590
Let me explain further.

1336
02:01:12,810 --> 02:01:17,290
The property of Marmaragcik
belongs to Osman Bey from now on

1337
02:01:21,050 --> 02:01:23,340
He took it from our enemy Olof.

1338
02:01:31,940 --> 02:01:34,330
Why are you so surprised, Kantakouzanos?

1339
02:01:34,440 --> 02:01:36,010
You must rejoice.

1340
02:02:09,930 --> 02:02:11,490
Brother!

1341
02:02:20,910 --> 02:02:22,660
Are you okay brother?

1342
02:02:22,660 --> 02:02:24,200
I'm fine my Bey.

1343
02:02:28,160 --> 02:02:29,660
Oh brother!

1344
02:02:31,840 --> 02:02:33,770
Praise be to Allah
who brought us together

1345
02:02:33,770 --> 02:02:35,370
Here is my brother!

1346
02:02:35,380 --> 02:02:36,950
Don't worry, brother.

1347
02:02:37,030 --> 02:02:38,820
We are wounded too.

1348
02:02:46,780 --> 02:02:48,280
Turgut Bey.

1349
02:02:48,570 --> 02:02:50,120
May Allah bless you.

1350
02:02:50,500 --> 02:02:52,060
Eyvallah.

1351
02:03:04,350 --> 02:03:05,850
Reymos.

1352
02:03:08,040 --> 02:03:10,580
All the trouble came from
those dogs.

1353
02:03:11,670 --> 02:03:13,170
Listen carefully.

1354
02:03:14,060 --> 02:03:16,070
This will be the last you hear from them.

1355
02:03:24,290 --> 02:03:25,820
Tell me now!

1356
02:03:27,190 --> 02:03:29,460
So that I cut your head
at once!

1357
02:03:31,630 --> 02:03:33,190
Which one?

1358
02:03:34,660 --> 02:03:36,680
Do you want to hear how
we raided the town?

1359
02:03:37,930 --> 02:03:40,450
How we killed your men?

1360
02:03:44,000 --> 02:03:47,500
How we killed Batur?

1361
02:03:48,080 --> 02:03:53,300
Or how we put the whole blame on you?

1362
02:03:57,940 --> 02:04:00,950
This will be your last war Osman.

1363
02:04:01,830 --> 02:04:03,880
You will always attack.

1364
02:04:04,770 --> 02:04:07,280
But we will be the ones beating you.

1365
02:04:07,960 --> 02:04:10,510
You say this is the last war, right?

1366
02:04:11,640 --> 02:04:14,160
This is a war between right and wrong.

1367
02:04:14,620 --> 02:04:17,180
It will go on forever.

1368
02:04:18,000 --> 02:04:19,850
But you won't be able to see it.

1369
02:04:43,840 --> 02:04:45,430
Allah is the greatest!

1370
02:04:45,670 --> 02:04:47,210
Allah is the greatest!

1371
02:04:47,430 --> 02:04:48,970
Allah is the greatest!

1372
02:04:49,070 --> 02:04:52,140
Allah is the greatest!

1373
02:04:52,140 --> 02:04:53,700
Allah is the greatest

1374
02:05:13,150 --> 02:05:14,950
Remus is a good commander.

1375
02:05:16,780 --> 02:05:18,590
And he knows all the truth.

1376
02:05:20,470 --> 02:05:23,480
And he knows the tricks
that Olof pulls.

1377
02:05:24,430 --> 02:05:26,260
Take him to prison now.

1378
02:05:27,200 --> 02:05:29,240
He has something to tell me.

1379
02:05:41,360 --> 02:05:43,890
My Bey,
Olof and the rest are about to arrive.

1380
02:05:43,890 --> 02:05:45,450
Their number is large.

1381
02:06:00,200 --> 02:06:01,940
Come now.

1382
02:06:02,580 --> 02:06:04,160
Close the gates!

1383
02:06:04,440 --> 02:06:06,250
Archers, to the top!

1384
02:06:10,150 --> 02:06:11,720
Come on.

1385
02:06:18,070 --> 02:06:19,420
Come to us.

1386
02:06:32,370 --> 02:06:34,140
Come on brothers!

1387
02:06:45,890 --> 02:06:47,450
Pull, come on!

1388
02:06:49,060 --> 02:06:50,810
Pull, come on!

1389
02:06:55,930 --> 02:06:57,480
Pull, come on!

1390
02:07:03,230 --> 02:07:04,810
You will die, Osman!

1391
02:07:11,470 --> 02:07:12,980
Archers!

1392
02:07:30,485 --> 02:07:32,795
The infidels attack with full force!

1393
02:07:32,925 --> 02:07:34,235
They are a single body!

1394
02:07:34,325 --> 02:07:36,215
The Islamic world cannot unite.

1395
02:07:36,275 --> 02:07:37,825
Mongols at one hand.

1396
02:07:37,855 --> 02:07:39,395
Crusaders on the other hand.

1397
02:07:39,405 --> 02:07:40,945
They are on the offensive side.

1398
02:07:41,035 --> 02:07:42,735
We are on the defensive side.

1399
02:07:43,175 --> 02:07:44,725
This is difficult to accept.

1400
02:07:45,855 --> 02:07:48,065
How can we eliminate this crisis,
Sheikh?

1401
02:07:49,985 --> 02:07:52,005
Prophet says...

1402
02:07:52,945 --> 02:07:57,735
....Allah is hardworking.
And He loves the hardworkers.

1403
02:07:57,975 --> 02:08:02,245
The universe is in motion.

1404
02:08:03,305 --> 02:08:04,895
Rivers become a waterfall.

1405
02:08:05,615 --> 02:08:09,185
Day becomes night,
and night becomes day

1406
02:08:09,855 --> 02:08:11,895
Seasons change.

1407
02:08:12,145 --> 02:08:13,855
The moon is going away.

1408
02:08:14,865 --> 02:08:16,615
And the sun shines.

1409
02:08:17,655 --> 02:08:19,205
Therefore...

1410
02:08:19,625 --> 02:08:23,975
God loves movement and action.

1411
02:08:24,325 --> 02:08:26,575
He loves the rebirth.

1412
02:08:27,095 --> 02:08:31,145
For this reason, Muslims must be alive.

1413
02:08:31,335 --> 02:08:33,675
And they must always be working.

1414
02:08:34,305 --> 02:08:38,355
Work is important, my dears.

1415
02:08:39,705 --> 02:08:42,215
It is, my friends.

1416
02:08:42,835 --> 02:08:44,355
It very is.

1417
02:08:48,225 --> 02:08:53,255
The Islamic world
has forgotten working.

1418
02:08:54,195 --> 02:08:59,215
We must kindle the flame of jihad
in our heart again.

1419
02:09:00,525 --> 02:09:02,905
So, are we going to make
the oppressors obey us?

1420
02:09:03,325 --> 02:09:05,055
With Allah's permission, yes.

1421
02:09:05,585 --> 02:09:07,645
What else should we do, my sheikh?

1422
02:09:07,835 --> 02:09:10,955
Surah At-Tawbah answers your question.

1423
02:09:11,135 --> 02:09:18,865
"O believers! What is the matter with you
that when you are asked to march forth...

1424
02:09:18,865 --> 02:09:23,165
...in the cause of Allah,
you cling firmly to the land?"
(Surah At-Tawbah 38)

1425
02:09:23,165 --> 02:09:26,215
This means our unity is broken.

1426
02:09:27,295 --> 02:09:31,795
What does Allah suggest us,
Prince Aladdin?

1427
02:09:32,395 --> 02:09:34,975
Allah Almighty says in Surah At-Tawbah...

1428
02:09:35,075 --> 02:09:41,075
"if you do not march forth, He will afflict you with
a painful torment and replace you with other people.

1429
02:09:41,075 --> 02:09:46,555
You are not harming Him in the least.
And Allah is Most Capable of everything."
(Surah At-Tawbah 39)

1430
02:09:47,495 --> 02:09:52,265
Who are the ones Allah loves, Prince Orhan?

1431
02:09:52,375 --> 02:09:54,465
Allah Almighty says in Surat Al-Saff...

1432
02:09:54,465 --> 02:10:00,205
"Surely Allah loves those who fight in His cause in
solid ranks as if they were one concrete structure."
(Surah As-Saf 4)

1433
02:10:00,585 --> 02:10:02,165
Praise e!

1434
02:10:02,555 --> 02:10:04,355
Praise be to you!

1435
02:10:05,175 --> 02:10:08,215
I don't need to lecture you!

1436
02:10:08,655 --> 02:10:11,445
You have all the answers!

1437
02:10:14,265 --> 02:10:20,245
For this reason,
we will get rid of laziness and work.

1438
02:10:23,105 --> 02:10:27,415
In the name of Allah the Merciful,
the Compassionate.

1439
02:10:27,645 --> 02:10:31,835
My Allah, do not put pressure on your
valiants who fight in your cause.

1440
02:10:32,395 --> 02:10:38,095
And they attack the enemy
when the morning comes.

1441
02:10:38,335 --> 02:10:40,335
Help them.

1442
02:10:40,935 --> 02:10:42,465
- Amen.
- Amen.

1443
02:10:42,465 --> 02:10:47,015
Do not let our valiants
be humiliated in front of the infidels.

1444
02:10:47,205 --> 02:10:48,755
- Amen.
- Amen.

1445
02:10:48,805 --> 02:10:53,505
Grant us victory over the infidels.

1446
02:10:53,545 --> 02:10:55,095
- Amen.
- Amen.

1447
02:10:55,105 --> 02:10:59,995
Let the Islamic world unite
against the infidels again.

1448
02:11:00,185 --> 02:11:01,555
Amen.

1449
02:11:01,575 --> 02:11:05,855
Make the Islamic world gain its glory again.

1450
02:11:05,955 --> 02:11:08,955
Let them become brothers, and unite.

1451
02:11:08,955 --> 02:11:10,295
- Amen.
- Amen.

1452
02:11:10,325 --> 02:11:13,845
May they become one body and be strong.

1453
02:11:14,265 --> 02:11:15,825
- Amen.
- Amen.

1454
02:11:17,805 --> 02:11:19,165
Amen.

1455
02:12:06,485 --> 02:12:09,215
I'll swing your head on these walls!

1456
02:12:12,275 --> 02:12:14,055
You are only talking!

1457
02:12:14,315 --> 02:12:16,145
But I perform!

1458
02:12:29,075 --> 02:12:30,575
No!

1459
02:12:30,715 --> 02:12:32,285
No!

1460
02:12:46,655 --> 02:12:49,185
The time for talking is over!

1461
02:12:49,885 --> 02:12:56,225
From now on, only the voice
of crying will be heard!

1462
02:12:56,995 --> 02:12:58,545
Osman!

1463
02:12:59,225 --> 02:13:01,035
Shout as long as you want!

1464
02:13:01,915 --> 02:13:05,475
Marmaracik Castle became
the property of the Turks

1465
02:13:05,725 --> 02:13:07,285
Allah is the greatest!

1466
02:13:07,445 --> 02:13:13,975
Allah is the greatest!

1467
02:13:13,995 --> 02:13:21,705
Allah is the greatest!

1468
02:13:21,715 --> 02:13:23,445
Allah is the greatest!

1469
02:13:23,515 --> 02:13:25,575
Allah is the greatest

